window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b066-3fe6c71c821a084b.json"]={sha256:"3fe6c71c821a084b05517e8b58a26f3b2af84933b9e840f564341dc5a042aa39",value:{"id":"b066","title":"高層建築調諧質量阻尼器","titleEn":"Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從超高層的橫風向渦流振動與居住舒適度出發，建立主結構模態與擺錘的雙自由度模型，依 Den Hartog 準則決定調頻與阻尼，再處理數百公噸質量塊的吊裝、現場調頻、阻尼器試驗、行程限制與長期監測，最後以台北 101 與上海中心大廈的實例比較油壓與渦電流兩種耗能方式。","summaryEn":"Starting from across-wind vortex shedding and occupant comfort in supertall towers, build a two-degree-of-freedom model of the building mode and pendulum, set tuning and damping with the Den Hartog criteria, then handle the erection of a mass of several hundred tonnes, on-site tuning, damper testing, stroke limits and long-term monitoring, comparing hydraulic and eddy-current dissipation through Taipei 101 and Shanghai Tower.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-tall-systems","subcategoryTitle":"高層結構系統與減振","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tall-building structural systems and damping","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-tall-systems","learningTags":["structures","st-tall-systems","damper"],"architectureFamily":"damper","architectureNodes":[["主結構第一模態","Building first mode"],["擺錘質量塊","Pendulum mass"],["吊索與調頻機構","Hangers and tuning hardware"],["黏滯或渦電流阻尼器","Viscous or eddy-current dampers"],["緩衝與行程限制","Buffers and stroke limits"],["監測與維護紀錄","Monitoring and maintenance records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[1,3],[1,4],[3,5],[0,5]],"diagram":{"type":"damper","labels":["主結構第一模態","擺錘質量塊","吊索與調頻機構","黏滯或渦電流阻尼器","緩衝與行程限制"],"labelsEn":["Building first mode","Pendulum mass","Hangers and tuning hardware","Viscous or eddy-current dampers","Buffers and stroke limits"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某超高層第一模態 f₁ = 0.140 Hz、結構阻尼 ζ_s = 1%、頂部廣義質量 M* = 100,000 t，選用 m_d = 660 t 擺錘。質量比 μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066；最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ) = 0.9934，阻尼器頻率 f_d = 0.140×0.9934 ≈ 0.139 Hz；最佳阻尼比 ζ_d = √[3μ/(8(1+μ)³)] = √[0.0198/8.159] ≈ 0.049；擺長 L = g/(2πf_d)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m；阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d ≈ 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m。以雙自由度模型掃頻，共振放大由 1/(2×0.01) = 50 降到約 13.6，相當於等效阻尼約 3.7%，風致加速度約降為原來的 √(1%/3.7%) ≈ 52%。若頻率偏離 5%，等效阻尼只剩約 2.1%。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: a supertall tower has f₁ = 0.140 Hz, structural damping ζ_s = 1% and a top generalised mass M* = 100,000 t, and a 660 t pendulum is chosen. The mass ratio is μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066; the optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ) = 0.9934, so f_d = 0.140×0.9934 ≈ 0.139 Hz; the optimum damping ratio is ζ_d = √[3μ/(8(1+μ)³)] = √[0.0198/8.159] ≈ 0.049; the pendulum length is L = g/(2πf_d)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m; the damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d ≈ 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m. A two-degree-of-freedom sweep lowers the resonant amplification from 1/(2×0.01) = 50 to about 13.6, equivalent to about 3.7% damping, so wind-induced acceleration falls to roughly √(1%/3.7%) ≈ 52% of the original. A 5% frequency offset leaves only about 2.1% equivalent damping. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b066-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「風致振動與居住舒適度」與「模態質量與雙自由度模型」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort\" and \"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b066-v13-01","title":"風致振動與居住舒適度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「頂層樓板加速度」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Top-floor acceleration” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"超高層建築的第一模態頻率常低於 0.2 Hz，風吹過方形或圓角斷面時，背風側交替脫落的渦流會產生垂直於風向的週期性橫風力；當渦流脫落頻率接近結構頻率時，橫風向振動被共振放大，通常比順風向擺動更大。這種擺動很少威脅強度，卻會讓高樓層的人感到暈眩、看到吊燈搖晃或聽到帷幕牆摩擦聲，因此設計目標常以「回歸期內頂層尖峰加速度」表示，而不是位移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「頂層樓板加速度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first-mode frequency of a supertall tower is often below 0.2 Hz. As wind flows past a square or rounded section, vortices shed alternately on the leeward side and produce a periodic across-wind force; when the shedding frequency approaches the structural frequency, across-wind motion is amplified by resonance and usually exceeds along-wind sway. This motion rarely threatens strength, but upper-floor occupants feel queasy, see pendant lights swing or hear façade joints creak, so the design target is usually a peak top-floor acceleration for a given return period rather than a displacement. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Top-floor acceleration” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：渦流脫落頻率 f_s = St·U/B。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Vortex-shedding frequency f_s = St·U/B.","failure":"常見誤解：「超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「頂層樓板加速度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Top-floor acceleration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-01-k1","title":"風致振動與居住舒適度","titleEn":"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort","text":"超高層建築的第一模態頻率常低於 0.2 Hz，風吹過方形或圓角斷面時，背風側交替脫落的渦流會產生垂直於風向的週期性橫風力；當渦流脫落頻率接近結構頻率時，橫風向振動被共振放大，通常比順風向擺動更大。這種擺動很少威脅強度，卻會讓高樓層的人感到暈眩、看到吊燈搖晃或聽到帷幕牆摩擦聲，因此設計目標常以「回歸期內頂層尖峰加速度」表示，而不是位移。","textEn":"The first-mode frequency of a supertall tower is often below 0.2 Hz. As wind flows past a square or rounded section, vortices shed alternately on the leeward side and produce a periodic across-wind force; when the shedding frequency approaches the structural frequency, across-wind motion is amplified by resonance and usually exceeds along-wind sway.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「風致振動與居住舒適度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort\" is correct?","options":["超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。","超高層建築的第一模態頻率常低於 0.2 Hz，風吹過方形或圓角斷面時，背風側交替脫落的渦流會產生垂直於風向的週期性橫風力。","阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened.","The first-mode frequency of a supertall tower is often below 0.2 Hz.","A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"超高層建築的第一模態頻率常低於 0.2 Hz，風吹過方形或圓角斷面時，背風側交替脫落的渦流會產生垂直於風向的週期性橫風力；當渦流脫落頻率接近結構頻率時，橫風向振動被共振放大，通常比順風向擺動更大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first-mode frequency of a supertall tower is often below 0.2 Hz. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b066-v13-02","title":"風致振動與居住舒適度：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂層樓板加速度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Top-floor acceleration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：渦流脫落頻率 f_s = St·U/B。取方形斷面 St ≈ 0.12、寬度 B = 50 m、結構頻率 f₁ = 0.14 Hz，臨界風速 U_cr = f₁·B/St = 0.14×50/0.12 ≈ 58 m/s；若改為斜角或退縮斷面使 St 分散，共振不再集中在單一風速。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Vortex-shedding frequency f_s = St·U/B. With a square-section St ≈ 0.12, width B = 50 m and structural frequency f₁ = 0.14 Hz, the critical wind speed is U_cr = f₁·B/St = 0.14×50/0.12 ≈ 58 m/s; chamfered or tapered sections spread St so resonance no longer locks onto one wind speed. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比對風洞高頻力平衡（HFFB）或氣動彈性模型試驗得到的橫風向力頻譜與本步估算的臨界風速，並把試驗換算到實尺度的頂層加速度，與居住性準則（例如以半年或一年回歸期計的尖峰加速度限值）逐一比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare the across-wind force spectrum from a high-frequency force-balance (HFFB) or aeroelastic wind-tunnel test with the critical wind speed estimated here, scale the test to full-size top-floor acceleration, and check it against habitability criteria such as peak-acceleration limits for a half-year or one-year return period.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"渦流脫落頻率 f_s = St·U/B。取方形斷面 St ≈ 0.12、寬度 B = 50 m、結構頻率 f₁ = 0.14 Hz，臨界風速 U_cr = f₁·B/St = 0.14×50/0.12 ≈ 58 m/s；若改為斜角或退縮斷面使 St 分散，共振不再集中在單一風速。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Vortex-shedding frequency f_s = St·U/B. With a square-section St ≈ 0.12, width B = 50 m and structural frequency f₁ = 0.14 Hz, the critical wind speed is U_cr = f₁·B/St = 0.14×50/0.12 ≈ 58 m/s; chamfered or tapered sections spread St so resonance no longer locks onto one wind speed. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「風致振動與居住舒適度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。","阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","渦流脫落頻率 f_s = St·U/B。"],"optionsEn":["The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction.","A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","Vortex-shedding frequency f_s = St·U/B."],"answer":2,"explanation":"渦流脫落頻率 f_s = St·U/B。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Vortex-shedding frequency f_s = St·U/B. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b066-v13-03","title":"風致振動與居住舒適度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂層樓板加速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Top-floor acceleration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比對風洞高頻力平衡（HFFB）或氣動彈性模型試驗得到的橫風向力頻譜與本步估算的臨界風速，並把試驗換算到實尺度的頂層加速度，與居住性準則（例如以半年或一年回歸期計的尖峰加速度限值）逐一比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare the across-wind force spectrum from a high-frequency force-balance (HFFB) or aeroelastic wind-tunnel test with the critical wind speed estimated here, scale the test to full-size top-floor acceleration, and check it against habitability criteria such as peak-acceleration limits for a half-year or one-year return period. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計階段就要在頂部機械層預留阻尼器的空間、樓板承載與維修動線，並在風洞報告中要求同時提供有無阻尼器兩種情境的加速度預測，作為業主決策依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Reserve damper space, slab capacity and maintenance access in the top mechanical levels from the design stage, and require the wind-tunnel report to predict accelerations both with and without a damper so the owner can decide.","failure":"注意干擾：若只做順風向靜力設計而忽略橫風向共振，結構強度合格，但完工後在中等強風就出現明顯擺動與住戶抱怨，事後才補裝阻尼器時，樓層空間、承載與吊裝路徑都已受限。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Designing only for along-wind static load and ignoring across-wind resonance passes strength checks, yet after completion moderate winds cause noticeable sway and complaints; retrofitting a damper then finds floor space, load capacity and lifting routes already constrained. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比對風洞高頻力平衡（HFFB）或氣動彈性模型試驗得到的橫風向力頻譜與本步估算的臨界風速，並把試驗換算到實尺度的頂層加速度，與居住性準則（例如以半年或一年回歸期計的尖峰加速度限值）逐一比較。","textEn":"Compare the across-wind force spectrum from a high-frequency force-balance (HFFB) or aeroelastic wind-tunnel test with the critical wind speed estimated here, scale the test to full-size top-floor acceleration, and check it against habitability criteria such as peak-acceleration limits for a half-year or one-year return period.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計階段就要在頂部機械層預留阻尼器的空間、樓板承載與維修動線，並在風洞報告中要求同時提供有無阻尼器兩種情境的加速度預測，作為業主決策依據。","textEn":"Reserve damper space, slab capacity and maintenance access in the top mechanical levels from the design stage, and require the wind-tunnel report to predict accelerations both with and without a damper so the owner can decide.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「風致振動與居住舒適度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort\"?","options":["比對風洞高頻力平衡（HFFB）或氣動彈性模型試驗得到的橫風向力頻譜與本步估算的臨界風速，並把試驗換算到實尺度的頂層加速度，與居住性準則（例如以半年或一年回歸期計的尖峰加速度限值）逐一比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。"],"optionsEn":["Compare the across-wind force spectrum from a high-frequency force-balance (HFFB) or aeroelastic wind-tunnel test with the critical wind speed estimated here, scale the test to full-size top-floor acceleration, and check it against habitability criteria such as peak-acceleration limits for a half-year or one-year return period.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比對風洞高頻力平衡（HFFB）或氣動彈性模型試驗得到的橫風向力頻譜與本步估算的臨界風速，並把試驗換算到實尺度的頂層加速度，與居住性準則（例如以半年或一年回歸期計的尖峰加速度限值）逐一比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare the across-wind force spectrum from a high-frequency force-balance (HFFB) or aeroelastic wind-tunnel test with the critical wind speed estimated here, scale the test to full-size top-floor acceleration, and check it against habitability criteria such as peak-acceleration limits for a half-year or one-year return period. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b066-v13-04","title":"風致振動與居住舒適度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂層樓板加速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Top-floor acceleration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只做順風向靜力設計而忽略橫風向共振，結構強度合格，但完工後在中等強風就出現明顯擺動與住戶抱怨，事後才補裝阻尼器時，樓層空間、承載與吊裝路徑都已受限。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Designing only for along-wind static load and ignoring across-wind resonance passes strength checks, yet after completion moderate winds cause noticeable sway and complaints; retrofitting a damper then finds floor space, load capacity and lifting routes already constrained. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這種擺動很少威脅強度，卻會讓高樓層的人感到暈眩、看到吊燈搖晃或聽到帷幕牆摩擦聲，因此設計目標常以「回歸期內頂層尖峰加速度」表示，而不是位移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This motion rarely threatens strength, but upper-floor occupants feel queasy, see pendant lights swing or hear façade joints creak, so the design target is usually a peak top-floor acceleration for a given return period rather than a displacement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只做順風向靜力設計而忽略橫風向共振，結構強度合格，但完工後在中等強風就出現明顯擺動與住戶抱怨，事後才補裝阻尼器時，樓層空間、承載與吊裝路徑都已受限。","textEn":"Designing only for along-wind static load and ignoring across-wind resonance passes strength checks, yet after completion moderate winds cause noticeable sway and complaints; retrofitting a damper then finds floor space, load capacity and lifting routes already constrained.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「風致振動與居住舒適度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind-induced motion and occupant comfort\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只做順風向靜力設計而忽略橫風向共振，結構強度合格，但完工後在中等強風就出現明顯擺動與住戶抱怨，事後才補裝阻尼器時，樓層空間、承載與吊裝路徑都已受限。","阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Designing only for along-wind static load and ignoring across-wind resonance passes strength checks, yet after completion moderate winds cause noticeable sway and complaints.","A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只做順風向靜力設計而忽略橫風向共振，結構強度合格，但完工後在中等強風就出現明顯擺動與住戶抱怨，事後才補裝阻尼器時，樓層空間、承載與吊裝路徑都已受限。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Designing only for along-wind static load and ignoring across-wind resonance passes strength checks, yet after completion moderate winds cause noticeable sway and complaints; retrofitting a damper then finds floor space, load capacity and lifting routes already constrained. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b066-v13-05","title":"模態質量與雙自由度模型：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「第一彎曲模態」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “First bending mode” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"調諧質量阻尼器只對準一個模態，因此先把建築在該模態下簡化為等效單自由度系統：等效質量是以阻尼器所在位置的模態位移正規化後的廣義質量，而不是整棟樓的總重。阻尼器質量除以這個廣義質量就是質量比 μ，它決定了阻尼器能提供的最大附加阻尼；把擺錘與主結構串成雙自由度系統後，原本單一共振峰會分裂成兩個較低的峰。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「第一彎曲模態」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A tuned mass damper targets a single mode, so the building is first reduced to an equivalent single-degree-of-freedom system for that mode. Its equivalent mass is the generalised mass normalised to the modal displacement at the damper location, not the total building weight. Damper mass divided by this generalised mass is the mass ratio μ, which bounds the added damping the device can supply; coupling the pendulum to the structure as a two-degree-of-freedom system splits the single resonance peak into two lower peaks. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “First bending mode” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：均勻懸臂第一模態以頂端位移正規化時，廣義質量約為總質量的 0.25。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a uniform cantilever normalised to tip displacement, the first-mode generalised mass is about 0.25 of the total mass.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「第一彎曲模態」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “First bending mode”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-05-k1","title":"模態質量與雙自由度模型","titleEn":"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model","text":"調諧質量阻尼器只對準一個模態，因此先把建築在該模態下簡化為等效單自由度系統：等效質量是以阻尼器所在位置的模態位移正規化後的廣義質量，而不是整棟樓的總重。阻尼器質量除以這個廣義質量就是質量比 μ，它決定了阻尼器能提供的最大附加阻尼；把擺錘與主結構串成雙自由度系統後，原本單一共振峰會分裂成兩個較低的峰。","textEn":"A tuned mass damper targets a single mode, so the building is first reduced to an equivalent single-degree-of-freedom system for that mode. Its equivalent mass is the generalised mass normalised to the modal displacement at the damper location, not the total building weight.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模態質量與雙自由度模型」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。","質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。","調諧質量阻尼器只對準一個模態，因此先把建築在該模態下簡化為等效單自由度系統：等效質量是以阻尼器所在位置的模態位移正規化後的廣義質量，而不是整棟樓的總重。"],"optionsEn":["A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight.","The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.","A tuned mass damper targets a single mode, so the building is first reduced to an equivalent single-degree-of-freedom system for that mode."],"answer":2,"explanation":"調諧質量阻尼器只對準一個模態，因此先把建築在該模態下簡化為等效單自由度系統：等效質量是以阻尼器所在位置的模態位移正規化後的廣義質量，而不是整棟樓的總重。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A tuned mass damper targets a single mode, so the building is first reduced to an equivalent single-degree-of-freedom system for that mode. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b066-v13-06","title":"模態質量與雙自由度模型：定量估算","titleEn":"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「第一彎曲模態」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “First bending mode” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：均勻懸臂第一模態以頂端位移正規化時，廣義質量約為總質量的 0.25。若參與擺動的質量取 400,000 t，M* ≈ 0.25×400,000 = 100,000 t；阻尼器 660 t 時 μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a uniform cantilever normalised to tip displacement, the first-mode generalised mass is about 0.25 of the total mass. Taking 400,000 t of participating mass gives M* ≈ 0.25×400,000 = 100,000 t; a 660 t damper then gives μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用有限元素模型取出阻尼器所在樓層的模態向量與廣義質量，與手算懸臂近似比較；再以雙自由度模型掃頻，確認加裝阻尼器後的頻率響應出現兩個峰且峰值低於無阻尼器時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Extract the modal vector and generalised mass at the damper floor from the finite-element model and compare with the hand cantilever estimate; then sweep the two-degree-of-freedom model to confirm that the response with the damper shows two peaks lower than the undamped peak.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"均勻懸臂第一模態以頂端位移正規化時，廣義質量約為總質量的 0.25。若參與擺動的質量取 400,000 t，M* ≈ 0.25×400,000 = 100,000 t；阻尼器 660 t 時 μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a uniform cantilever normalised to tip displacement, the first-mode generalised mass is about 0.25 of the total mass. Taking 400,000 t of participating mass gives M* ≈ 0.25×400,000 = 100,000 t; a 660 t damper then gives μ = 660/100,000 = 0.0066. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模態質量與雙自由度模型」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model\", which statement holds?","options":["均勻懸臂第一模態以頂端位移正規化時，廣義質量約為總質量的 0.25。","質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。","只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。"],"optionsEn":["For a uniform cantilever normalised to tip displacement, the first-mode generalised mass is about 0.25 of the total mass.","Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan.","Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻懸臂第一模態以頂端位移正規化時，廣義質量約為總質量的 0.25。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a uniform cantilever normalised to tip displacement, the first-mode generalised mass is about 0.25 of the total mass. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b066-v13-07","title":"模態質量與雙自由度模型：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「第一彎曲模態」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “First bending mode” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用有限元素模型取出阻尼器所在樓層的模態向量與廣義質量，與手算懸臂近似比較；再以雙自由度模型掃頻，確認加裝阻尼器後的頻率響應出現兩個峰且峰值低於無阻尼器時。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Extract the modal vector and generalised mass at the damper floor from the finite-element model and compare with the hand cantilever estimate; then sweep the two-degree-of-freedom model to confirm that the response with the damper shows two peaks lower than the undamped peak. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：阻尼器通常放在接近頂部、模態位移最大的樓層；若主要問題是第二模態或扭轉，需另行評估位置或採用多組阻尼器，並在結構計算書中寫明所針對的模態編號與方向。","observationEn":"Site practice: Dampers usually sit near the top where modal displacement peaks; if the problem is the second mode or torsion, re-evaluate the location or use several devices, and state the targeted mode number and direction in the structural calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：把整棟樓的總質量當成分母，會把質量比低估數倍，導致阻尼器設計過小；反之若把阻尼器放在模態位移小的樓層，等效質量變大，同一顆質量塊的效果大打折扣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total building mass as the denominator underestimates the mass ratio several-fold and undersizes the damper; conversely, placing the damper where the modal displacement is small inflates the equivalent mass and sharply reduces the benefit of the same block. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用有限元素模型取出阻尼器所在樓層的模態向量與廣義質量，與手算懸臂近似比較；再以雙自由度模型掃頻，確認加裝阻尼器後的頻率響應出現兩個峰且峰值低於無阻尼器時。","textEn":"Extract the modal vector and generalised mass at the damper floor from the finite-element model and compare with the hand cantilever estimate; then sweep the two-degree-of-freedom model to confirm that the response with the damper shows two peaks lower than the undamped peak.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"阻尼器通常放在接近頂部、模態位移最大的樓層；若主要問題是第二模態或扭轉，需另行評估位置或採用多組阻尼器，並在結構計算書中寫明所針對的模態編號與方向。","textEn":"Dampers usually sit near the top where modal displacement peaks; if the problem is the second mode or torsion, re-evaluate the location or use several devices, and state the targeted mode number and direction in the structural calculations.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模態質量與雙自由度模型」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用有限元素模型取出阻尼器所在樓層的模態向量與廣義質量，與手算懸臂近似比較；再以雙自由度模型掃頻，確認加裝阻尼器後的頻率響應出現兩個峰且峰值低於無阻尼器時。","阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Extract the modal vector and generalised mass at the damper floor from the finite-element model and compare with the hand cantilever estimate.","A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用有限元素模型取出阻尼器所在樓層的模態向量與廣義質量，與手算懸臂近似比較；再以雙自由度模型掃頻，確認加裝阻尼器後的頻率響應出現兩個峰且峰值低於無阻尼器時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Extract the modal vector and generalised mass at the damper floor from the finite-element model and compare with the hand cantilever estimate; then sweep the two-degree-of-freedom model to confirm that the response with the damper shows two peaks lower than the undamped peak. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b066-v13-08","title":"模態質量與雙自由度模型：失效診斷","titleEn":"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「第一彎曲模態」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “First bending mode” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整棟樓的總質量當成分母，會把質量比低估數倍，導致阻尼器設計過小；反之若把阻尼器放在模態位移小的樓層，等效質量變大，同一顆質量塊的效果大打折扣。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total building mass as the denominator underestimates the mass ratio several-fold and undersizes the damper; conversely, placing the damper where the modal displacement is small inflates the equivalent mass and sharply reduces the benefit of the same block. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：阻尼器質量除以這個廣義質量就是質量比 μ，它決定了阻尼器能提供的最大附加阻尼；把擺錘與主結構串成雙自由度系統後，原本單一共振峰會分裂成兩個較低的峰。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Damper mass divided by this generalised mass is the mass ratio μ, which bounds the added damping the device can supply; coupling the pendulum to the structure as a two-degree-of-freedom system splits the single resonance peak into two lower peaks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整棟樓的總質量當成分母，會把質量比低估數倍，導致阻尼器設計過小；反之若把阻尼器放在模態位移小的樓層，等效質量變大，同一顆質量塊的效果大打折扣。","textEn":"Using total building mass as the denominator underestimates the mass ratio several-fold and undersizes the damper; conversely, placing the damper where the modal displacement is small inflates the equivalent mass and sharply reduces the benefit of the same block.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模態質量與雙自由度模型」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Modal mass and the two-degree-of-freedom model\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。","把整棟樓的總質量當成分母，會把質量比低估數倍，導致阻尼器設計過小；反之若把阻尼器放在模態位移小的樓層，等效質量變大，同一顆質量塊的效果大打折扣。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.","Using total building mass as the denominator underestimates the mass ratio several-fold and undersizes the damper."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把整棟樓的總質量當成分母，會把質量比低估數倍，導致阻尼器設計過小；反之若把阻尼器放在模態位移小的樓層，等效質量變大，同一顆質量塊的效果大打折扣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total building mass as the denominator underestimates the mass ratio several-fold and undersizes the damper; conversely, placing the damper where the modal displacement is small inflates the equivalent mass and sharply reduces the benefit of the same block. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b066-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何」與「耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry\" and \"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b066-v13-09","title":"擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「擺錘質量塊與吊索」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pendulum mass and hangers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大型阻尼器常做成單擺：質量塊由多組鋼索或鋼棒懸吊，擺動頻率只由有效擺長與重力加速度決定，與質量本身無關。這讓設計者能用擺長調頻，但低頻需要很長的擺長；當樓層高度不足時，可用多段折返擺、加裝水平彈簧或倒擺組合縮短實體高度。質量塊多以厚鋼板疊合，以便分件吊運並在現場組成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「擺錘質量塊與吊索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Large dampers are often simple pendulums: the mass hangs from several sets of steel cables or rods, and the swing frequency depends only on the effective length and gravity, not on the mass. Designers can therefore tune by length, but low frequencies need long pendulums; when storey height is insufficient, folded multi-stage pendulums, horizontal springs or inverted-pendulum combinations shorten the physical height. The mass is usually built from stacked thick steel plates so it can be lifted in pieces and assembled on site. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Pendulum mass and hangers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單擺 f = (1/2π)·√(g/L)，故 L = g/(2πf)²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a simple pendulum f = (1/2π)·√(g/L), so L = g/(2πf)².","failure":"常見誤解：「質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「擺錘質量塊與吊索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Pendulum mass and hangers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-09-k1","title":"擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何","titleEn":"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry","text":"大型阻尼器常做成單擺：質量塊由多組鋼索或鋼棒懸吊，擺動頻率只由有效擺長與重力加速度決定，與質量本身無關。這讓設計者能用擺長調頻，但低頻需要很長的擺長；當樓層高度不足時，可用多段折返擺、加裝水平彈簧或倒擺組合縮短實體高度。","textEn":"Large dampers are often simple pendulums: the mass hangs from several sets of steel cables or rods, and the swing frequency depends only on the effective length and gravity, not on the mass. Designers can therefore tune by length, but low frequencies need long pendulums; when storey height is insufficient, folded multi-stage pendulums, horizontal springs or inverted-pendulum combinations shorten the physical height.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry\" is correct?","options":["大型阻尼器常做成單擺：質量塊由多組鋼索或鋼棒懸吊，擺動頻率只由有效擺長與重力加速度決定，與質量本身無關。","質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。","阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Large dampers are often simple pendulums: the mass hangs from several sets of steel cables or rods, and the swing frequency depends only on the effective length and gravity, not on the mass.","The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.","The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大型阻尼器常做成單擺：質量塊由多組鋼索或鋼棒懸吊，擺動頻率只由有效擺長與重力加速度決定，與質量本身無關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Large dampers are often simple pendulums: the mass hangs from several sets of steel cables or rods, and the swing frequency depends only on the effective length and gravity, not on the mass. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b066-v13-10","title":"擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何：定量估算","titleEn":"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「擺錘質量塊與吊索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pendulum mass and hangers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單擺 f = (1/2π)·√(g/L)，故 L = g/(2πf)²。目標頻率 0.139 Hz 時 L = 9.81/(2π×0.139)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m；若頻率改為 0.20 Hz，L 只需約 6.2 m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a simple pendulum f = (1/2π)·√(g/L), so L = g/(2πf)². A 0.139 Hz target gives L = 9.81/(2π×0.139)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m; a 0.20 Hz target needs only about 6.2 m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以小振幅自由擺動量測擺錘週期（記錄至少 10 個週期取平均），換算有效擺長，並與吊點幾何與吊索伸長量計算比較；吊索張力以應變計或液壓千斤頂讀值確認各吊索受力均勻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the pendulum period from small free swings, averaging at least 10 cycles, convert to effective length, and compare with the hanger geometry and cable-stretch calculation; confirm equal hanger forces with strain gauges or hydraulic-jack readings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單擺 f = (1/2π)·√(g/L)，故 L = g/(2πf)²。目標頻率 0.139 Hz 時 L = 9.81/(2π×0.139)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m；若頻率改為 0.20 Hz，L 只需約 6.2 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a simple pendulum f = (1/2π)·√(g/L), so L = g/(2πf)². A 0.139 Hz target gives L = 9.81/(2π×0.139)² = 9.81/0.763 ≈ 12.9 m; a 0.20 Hz target needs only about 6.2 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","單擺 f = (1/2π)·√(g/L)，故 L = g/(2πf)²。","阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。"],"optionsEn":["A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","For a simple pendulum f = (1/2π)·√(g/L), so L = g/(2πf)².","Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單擺 f = (1/2π)·√(g/L)，故 L = g/(2πf)²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a simple pendulum f = (1/2π)·√(g/L), so L = g/(2πf)². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b066-v13-11","title":"擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「擺錘質量塊與吊索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pendulum mass and hangers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以小振幅自由擺動量測擺錘週期（記錄至少 10 個週期取平均），換算有效擺長，並與吊點幾何與吊索伸長量計算比較；吊索張力以應變計或液壓千斤頂讀值確認各吊索受力均勻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the pendulum period from small free swings, averaging at least 10 cycles, convert to effective length, and compare with the hanger geometry and cable-stretch calculation; confirm equal hanger forces with strain gauges or hydraulic-jack readings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：質量塊分件設計時，每一片的重量要配合塔吊在該半徑的額定荷重與樓板臨時支撐，組裝順序寫入施工計畫；吊索端錨與吊點須設計成可檢查與可更換。","observationEn":"Site practice: When splitting the mass into pieces, size each plate to the tower-crane rating at that radius and to temporary slab shoring, write the assembly order into the construction plan, and make hanger terminations and pick points inspectable and replaceable.","failure":"注意干擾：吊索受力不均會讓質量塊傾斜並引入扭擺耦合，量到的頻率出現兩個相近峰值；若吊點連接或吊索端錨疲勞，長期擺動會造成鬆弛，頻率逐年漂移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unequal hanger forces tilt the mass and introduce torsional coupling, so the measured frequency shows two close peaks; fatigue at hanger connections or terminations lets long-term swinging cause slack and a frequency that drifts year by year. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以小振幅自由擺動量測擺錘週期（記錄至少 10 個週期取平均），換算有效擺長，並與吊點幾何與吊索伸長量計算比較；吊索張力以應變計或液壓千斤頂讀值確認各吊索受力均勻。","textEn":"Measure the pendulum period from small free swings, averaging at least 10 cycles, convert to effective length, and compare with the hanger geometry and cable-stretch calculation; confirm equal hanger forces with strain gauges or hydraulic-jack readings.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"質量塊分件設計時，每一片的重量要配合塔吊在該半徑的額定荷重與樓板臨時支撐，組裝順序寫入施工計畫；吊索端錨與吊點須設計成可檢查與可更換。","textEn":"When splitting the mass into pieces, size each plate to the tower-crane rating at that radius and to temporary slab shoring, write the assembly order into the construction plan, and make hanger terminations and pick points inspectable and replaceable.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。","以小振幅自由擺動量測擺錘週期（記錄至少 10 個週期取平均），換算有效擺長，並與吊點幾何與吊索伸長量計算比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring.","Measure the pendulum period from small free swings, averaging at least 10 cycles, convert to effective length, and compare with the hanger geometry and cable-stretch calculation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以小振幅自由擺動量測擺錘週期（記錄至少 10 個週期取平均），換算有效擺長，並與吊點幾何與吊索伸長量計算比較；吊索張力以應變計或液壓千斤頂讀值確認各吊索受力均勻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the pendulum period from small free swings, averaging at least 10 cycles, convert to effective length, and compare with the hanger geometry and cable-stretch calculation; confirm equal hanger forces with strain gauges or hydraulic-jack readings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b066-v13-12","title":"擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「擺錘質量塊與吊索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pendulum mass and hangers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"吊索受力不均會讓質量塊傾斜並引入扭擺耦合，量到的頻率出現兩個相近峰值；若吊點連接或吊索端錨疲勞，長期擺動會造成鬆弛，頻率逐年漂移。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unequal hanger forces tilt the mass and introduce torsional coupling, so the measured frequency shows two close peaks; fatigue at hanger connections or terminations lets long-term swinging cause slack and a frequency that drifts year by year. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：質量塊多以厚鋼板疊合，以便分件吊運並在現場組成。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The mass is usually built from stacked thick steel plates so it can be lifted in pieces and assembled on site.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"吊索受力不均會讓質量塊傾斜並引入扭擺耦合，量到的頻率出現兩個相近峰值；若吊點連接或吊索端錨疲勞，長期擺動會造成鬆弛，頻率逐年漂移。","textEn":"Unequal hanger forces tilt the mass and introduce torsional coupling, so the measured frequency shows two close peaks; fatigue at hanger connections or terminations lets long-term swinging cause slack and a frequency that drifts year by year.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擺錘頻率與懸吊幾何」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pendulum frequency and suspension geometry\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["吊索受力不均會讓質量塊傾斜並引入扭擺耦合，量到的頻率出現兩個相近峰值；若吊點連接或吊索端錨疲勞，長期擺動會造成鬆弛，頻率逐年漂移。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Unequal hanger forces tilt the mass and introduce torsional coupling, so the measured frequency shows two close peaks.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"吊索受力不均會讓質量塊傾斜並引入扭擺耦合，量到的頻率出現兩個相近峰值；若吊點連接或吊索端錨疲勞，長期擺動會造成鬆弛，頻率逐年漂移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unequal hanger forces tilt the mass and introduce torsional coupling, so the measured frequency shows two close peaks; fatigue at hanger connections or terminations lets long-term swinging cause slack and a frequency that drifts year by year. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b066-v13-13","title":"耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"擺錘只負責與結構反相運動，真正把能量變成熱的是連接擺錘與樓板的阻尼元件。油壓黏滯阻尼器讓矽油通過活塞孔口，阻尼力與速度的 α 次方成正比；渦電流阻尼器則讓磁鐵在銅板上方移動，感應電流產生與速度成正比的拖曳力，沒有流體密封，改變磁鐵與銅板的間隙即可調整阻尼。兩者都必須在極低速度與毫米級振幅下仍能作用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The pendulum only moves out of phase with the structure; the damping device between the pendulum and the floor turns energy into heat. A hydraulic viscous damper forces silicone fluid through piston orifices, giving a force proportional to velocity raised to the power α; an eddy-current damper moves magnets over a copper plate so induced currents create a drag proportional to velocity, with no fluid seals and with damping adjusted by the magnet–plate gap. Both must work at very low velocities and millimetre amplitudes. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：最佳阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The optimum damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-13-k1","title":"耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流","titleEn":"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current","text":"擺錘只負責與結構反相運動，真正把能量變成熱的是連接擺錘與樓板的阻尼元件。油壓黏滯阻尼器讓矽油通過活塞孔口，阻尼力與速度的 α 次方成正比；渦電流阻尼器則讓磁鐵在銅板上方移動，感應電流產生與速度成正比的拖曳力，沒有流體密封，改變磁鐵與銅板的間隙即可調整阻尼。","textEn":"The pendulum only moves out of phase with the structure; the damping device between the pendulum and the floor turns energy into heat. A hydraulic viscous damper forces silicone fluid through piston orifices, giving a force proportional to velocity raised to the power α; an eddy-current damper moves magnets over a copper plate so induced currents create a drag proportional to velocity, with no fluid seals and with damping adjusted by the magnet–plate gap.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。","擺錘只負責與結構反相運動，真正把能量變成熱的是連接擺錘與樓板的阻尼元件。","質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。"],"optionsEn":["The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction.","The pendulum only moves out of phase with the structure; the damping device between the pendulum and the floor turns energy into heat.","Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擺錘只負責與結構反相運動，真正把能量變成熱的是連接擺錘與樓板的阻尼元件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The pendulum only moves out of phase with the structure; the damping device between the pendulum and the floor turns energy into heat. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b066-v13-14","title":"耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流：定量估算","titleEn":"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：最佳阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d。取 m_d = 660,000 kg、ζ_d = 0.049、ω_d = 2π×0.139 = 0.873 rad/s，c_d = 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m；若擺錘速度 0.2 m/s，總阻尼力約 11.3 kN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The optimum damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d. With m_d = 660,000 kg, ζ_d = 0.049 and ω_d = 2π×0.139 = 0.873 rad/s, c_d = 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m; at a pendulum velocity of 0.2 m/s the total damping force is about 11.3 kN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：阻尼器出廠前以試驗機做正弦力—速度試驗，涵蓋設計頻率附近多個振幅與溫度，繪出遲滯迴圈計算等效阻尼係數，與規格允差（例如 ±15%）比較；渦電流阻尼則量測不同間隙下的拖曳力曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before delivery, test each damper on a rig with sinusoidal force–velocity runs at several amplitudes and temperatures near the design frequency, compute the equivalent damping coefficient from the hysteresis loops and compare with the specified tolerance such as ±15%; for eddy-current units, measure drag curves at several gaps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"最佳阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d。取 m_d = 660,000 kg、ζ_d = 0.049、ω_d = 2π×0.139 = 0.873 rad/s，c_d = 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m；若擺錘速度 0.2 m/s，總阻尼力約 11.3 kN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The optimum damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d. With m_d = 660,000 kg, ζ_d = 0.049 and ω_d = 2π×0.139 = 0.873 rad/s, c_d = 2×0.049×660,000×0.873 ≈ 56,500 N·s/m; at a pendulum velocity of 0.2 m/s the total damping force is about 11.3 kN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current\", which statement holds?","options":["只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。","阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。","最佳阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d。"],"optionsEn":["Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption.","A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.","The optimum damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最佳阻尼係數 c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The optimum damping coefficient is c_d = 2ζ_d·m_d·ω_d. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b066-v13-15","title":"耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"阻尼器出廠前以試驗機做正弦力—速度試驗，涵蓋設計頻率附近多個振幅與溫度，繪出遲滯迴圈計算等效阻尼係數，與規格允差（例如 ±15%）比較；渦電流阻尼則量測不同間隙下的拖曳力曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before delivery, test each damper on a rig with sinusoidal force–velocity runs at several amplitudes and temperatures near the design frequency, compute the equivalent damping coefficient from the hysteresis loops and compare with the specified tolerance such as ±15%; for eddy-current units, measure drag curves at several gaps. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：採購規範要寫明低速啟動門檻、溫度範圍內的阻尼變化上限與耐久循環次數，並要求原型試驗與逐件試驗報告；渦電流方案需另檢查磁鐵固定與銅板散熱。","observationEn":"Site practice: The procurement specification should state the low-velocity breakaway threshold, the maximum change of damping over the temperature range and the endurance cycles, and require prototype and production test reports; eddy-current designs also need checks on magnet retention and copper-plate heat dissipation.","failure":"注意干擾：黏滯阻尼器密封老化漏油會使阻尼係數下降、擺錘過度擺動；摩擦過大的導軌或密封則讓微小振幅時阻尼器「卡住」，阻尼器變成附加質量，平常強風幾乎沒有減振效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Aged seals that leak oil reduce the damping coefficient and let the pendulum over-swing; excessive friction in guides or seals makes the damper stick at small amplitudes so it behaves like added mass and gives almost no reduction in ordinary strong winds. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"阻尼器出廠前以試驗機做正弦力—速度試驗，涵蓋設計頻率附近多個振幅與溫度，繪出遲滯迴圈計算等效阻尼係數，與規格允差（例如 ±15%）比較；渦電流阻尼則量測不同間隙下的拖曳力曲線。","textEn":"Before delivery, test each damper on a rig with sinusoidal force–velocity runs at several amplitudes and temperatures near the design frequency, compute the equivalent damping coefficient from the hysteresis loops and compare with the specified tolerance such as ±15%; for eddy-current units, measure drag curves at several gaps.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"採購規範要寫明低速啟動門檻、溫度範圍內的阻尼變化上限與耐久循環次數，並要求原型試驗與逐件試驗報告；渦電流方案需另檢查磁鐵固定與銅板散熱。","textEn":"The procurement specification should state the low-velocity breakaway threshold, the maximum change of damping over the temperature range and the endurance cycles, and require prototype and production test reports; eddy-current designs also need checks on magnet retention and copper-plate heat dissipation.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current\"?","options":["阻尼器出廠前以試驗機做正弦力—速度試驗，涵蓋設計頻率附近多個振幅與溫度，繪出遲滯迴圈計算等效阻尼係數，與規格允差（例如 ±15%）比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。"],"optionsEn":["Before delivery, test each damper on a rig with sinusoidal force–velocity runs at several amplitudes and temperatures near the design frequency, compute the equivalent damping coefficient from the hysteresis loops and compare with the specified tolerance such as ±15%.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼器出廠前以試驗機做正弦力—速度試驗，涵蓋設計頻率附近多個振幅與溫度，繪出遲滯迴圈計算等效阻尼係數，與規格允差（例如 ±15%）比較；渦電流阻尼則量測不同間隙下的拖曳力曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before delivery, test each damper on a rig with sinusoidal force–velocity runs at several amplitudes and temperatures near the design frequency, compute the equivalent damping coefficient from the hysteresis loops and compare with the specified tolerance such as ±15%; for eddy-current units, measure drag curves at several gaps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b066-v13-16","title":"耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏滯阻尼器與渦電流板」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Viscous dampers and eddy-current plates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"黏滯阻尼器密封老化漏油會使阻尼係數下降、擺錘過度擺動；摩擦過大的導軌或密封則讓微小振幅時阻尼器「卡住」，阻尼器變成附加質量，平常強風幾乎沒有減振效果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Aged seals that leak oil reduce the damping coefficient and let the pendulum over-swing; excessive friction in guides or seals makes the damper stick at small amplitudes so it behaves like added mass and gives almost no reduction in ordinary strong winds. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：兩者都必須在極低速度與毫米級振幅下仍能作用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Both must work at very low velocities and millimetre amplitudes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"黏滯阻尼器密封老化漏油會使阻尼係數下降、擺錘過度擺動；摩擦過大的導軌或密封則讓微小振幅時阻尼器「卡住」，阻尼器變成附加質量，平常強風幾乎沒有減振效果。","textEn":"Aged seals that leak oil reduce the damping coefficient and let the pendulum over-swing; excessive friction in guides or seals makes the damper stick at small amplitudes so it behaves like added mass and gives almost no reduction in ordinary strong winds.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「耗能元件：油壓黏滯與渦電流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dissipation devices: viscous fluid and eddy current\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","黏滯阻尼器密封老化漏油會使阻尼係數下降、擺錘過度擺動；摩擦過大的導軌或密封則讓微小振幅時阻尼器「卡住」，阻尼器變成附加質量，平常強風幾乎沒有減振效果。","質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Aged seals that leak oil reduce the damping coefficient and let the pendulum over-swing.","Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan."],"answer":1,"explanation":"黏滯阻尼器密封老化漏油會使阻尼係數下降、擺錘過度擺動；摩擦過大的導軌或密封則讓微小振幅時阻尼器「卡住」，阻尼器變成附加質量，平常強風幾乎沒有減振效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Aged seals that leak oil reduce the damping coefficient and let the pendulum over-swing; excessive friction in guides or seals makes the damper stick at small amplitudes so it behaves like added mass and gives almost no reduction in ordinary strong winds. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b066-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「高空吊裝與分件組裝」與「實測頻率與現場調頻」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly\" and \"Measured frequency and on-site tuning\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b066-v13-17","title":"高空吊裝與分件組裝：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Plate-by-plate lifting route” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"數百公噸的質量塊無法一次吊上數百公尺高空，必須在結構封頂前把鋼板分件吊到預留樓層，再於臨時支撐上焊接或螺栓組成整體。吊裝期間樓板承受集中荷重，懸吊系統尚未受力，因此需要臨時支架承托質量塊；完成組裝後再逐步把荷重由臨時支架轉移到吊索，這個轉移過程決定了吊索初始張力是否均勻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A mass of several hundred tonnes cannot be hoisted to several hundred metres in one lift, so steel plates are raised piece by piece to the reserved floors before the structure is topped out, then welded or bolted together on temporary supports. During this phase the slab carries concentrated loads while the suspension is not yet loaded, so temporary frames hold the mass; after assembly the load is transferred step by step from the frames to the hangers, and this transfer determines whether the initial hanger tensions are even. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Plate-by-plate lifting route” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：質量 660 t 分成 41 片時，平均每片約 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t；若塔吊在 30 m 半徑的額定荷重為 20 t，扣除吊具 1.5 t 後仍有約 2.4 t 餘裕。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Splitting 660 t into 41 plates gives about 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t each; with a 20 t tower-crane rating at 30 m radius and 1.5 t of rigging, about 2.4 t of margin remains.","failure":"常見誤解：「質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Plate-by-plate lifting route”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-17-k1","title":"高空吊裝與分件組裝","titleEn":"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly","text":"數百公噸的質量塊無法一次吊上數百公尺高空，必須在結構封頂前把鋼板分件吊到預留樓層，再於臨時支撐上焊接或螺栓組成整體。吊裝期間樓板承受集中荷重，懸吊系統尚未受力，因此需要臨時支架承托質量塊；完成組裝後再逐步把荷重由臨時支架轉移到吊索，這個轉移過程決定了吊索初始張力是否均勻。","textEn":"A mass of several hundred tonnes cannot be hoisted to several hundred metres in one lift, so steel plates are raised piece by piece to the reserved floors before the structure is topped out, then welded or bolted together on temporary supports. During this phase the slab carries concentrated loads while the suspension is not yet loaded, so temporary frames hold the mass; after assembly the load is transferred step by step from the frames to the hangers, and this transfer determines whether the initial hanger tensions are even.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高空吊裝與分件組裝」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly\" is correct?","options":["質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。","阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","數百公噸的質量塊無法一次吊上數百公尺高空，必須在結構封頂前把鋼板分件吊到預留樓層，再於臨時支撐上焊接或螺栓組成整體。"],"optionsEn":["Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan.","A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","A mass of several hundred tonnes cannot be hoisted to several hundred metres in one lift, so steel plates are raised piece by piece to the reserved floors before the structure is topped out, then welded or bolted together on temporary supports."],"answer":2,"explanation":"數百公噸的質量塊無法一次吊上數百公尺高空，必須在結構封頂前把鋼板分件吊到預留樓層，再於臨時支撐上焊接或螺栓組成整體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A mass of several hundred tonnes cannot be hoisted to several hundred metres in one lift, so steel plates are raised piece by piece to the reserved floors before the structure is topped out, then welded or bolted together on temporary supports. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b066-v13-18","title":"高空吊裝與分件組裝：定量估算","titleEn":"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Plate-by-plate lifting route” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：質量 660 t 分成 41 片時，平均每片約 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t；若塔吊在 30 m 半徑的額定荷重為 20 t，扣除吊具 1.5 t 後仍有約 2.4 t 餘裕。臨時支架若以 8 支柱承托，每支約 81 t。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Splitting 660 t into 41 plates gives about 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t each; with a 20 t tower-crane rating at 30 m radius and 1.5 t of rigging, about 2.4 t of margin remains. Eight temporary posts would each carry about 81 t. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對每一吊次的重量、半徑與塔吊荷重表，吊裝前由第三方確認吊具；荷重轉移時以液壓千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計同步記錄，並量測質量塊水平度與各支架卸載量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check each lift's weight and radius against the crane load chart and have rigging verified by a third party; during load transfer, record jack pressures and hanger strain gauges together and measure the block's levelness and the unloading of each frame.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"質量 660 t 分成 41 片時，平均每片約 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t；若塔吊在 30 m 半徑的額定荷重為 20 t，扣除吊具 1.5 t 後仍有約 2.4 t 餘裕。臨時支架若以 8 支柱承托，每支約 81 t。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Splitting 660 t into 41 plates gives about 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t each; with a 20 t tower-crane rating at 30 m radius and 1.5 t of rigging, about 2.4 t of margin remains. Eight temporary posts would each carry about 81 t. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高空吊裝與分件組裝」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly\", which statement holds?","options":["質量 660 t 分成 41 片時，平均每片約 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t。","阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。","阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。"],"optionsEn":["Splitting 660 t into 41 plates gives about 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t each.","Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building.","A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"質量 660 t 分成 41 片時，平均每片約 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t；若塔吊在 30 m 半徑的額定荷重為 20 t，扣除吊具 1.5 t 後仍有約 2.4 t 餘裕。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Splitting 660 t into 41 plates gives about 660/41 ≈ 16.1 t each; with a 20 t tower-crane rating at 30 m radius and 1.5 t of rigging, about 2.4 t of margin remains. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b066-v13-19","title":"高空吊裝與分件組裝：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Plate-by-plate lifting route” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對每一吊次的重量、半徑與塔吊荷重表，吊裝前由第三方確認吊具；荷重轉移時以液壓千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計同步記錄，並量測質量塊水平度與各支架卸載量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check each lift's weight and radius against the crane load chart and have rigging verified by a third party; during load transfer, record jack pressures and hanger strain gauges together and measure the block's levelness and the unloading of each frame. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫應包含吊次清單、樓板臨時支撐計算、荷重轉移的分級步驟與停止條件（例如任一吊索張力偏差超過 10% 即暫停調整），並由結構設計者簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction plan should include a lift schedule, slab shoring calculations, staged load-transfer steps with hold points (for example pause and adjust if any hanger tension deviates by more than 10%), signed off by the structural designer.","failure":"注意干擾：若荷重轉移時某支吊索先受力，質量塊會傾斜並在吊點產生超過設計值的局部應力；臨時支架移除順序錯誤也可能造成樓板局部超載與裂縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If one hanger picks up load first during transfer, the block tilts and local stresses at its pick point exceed design values; removing temporary frames in the wrong order can locally overload and crack the slab. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對每一吊次的重量、半徑與塔吊荷重表，吊裝前由第三方確認吊具；荷重轉移時以液壓千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計同步記錄，並量測質量塊水平度與各支架卸載量。","textEn":"Check each lift's weight and radius against the crane load chart and have rigging verified by a third party; during load transfer, record jack pressures and hanger strain gauges together and measure the block's levelness and the unloading of each frame.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫應包含吊次清單、樓板臨時支撐計算、荷重轉移的分級步驟與停止條件（例如任一吊索張力偏差超過 10% 即暫停調整），並由結構設計者簽認。","textEn":"The construction plan should include a lift schedule, slab shoring calculations, staged load-transfer steps with hold points (for example pause and adjust if any hanger tension deviates by more than 10%), signed off by the structural designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高空吊裝與分件組裝」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","核對每一吊次的重量、半徑與塔吊荷重表，吊裝前由第三方確認吊具；荷重轉移時以液壓千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計同步記錄，並量測質量塊水平度與各支架卸載量。","阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Check each lift's weight and radius against the crane load chart and have rigging verified by a third party.","A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核對每一吊次的重量、半徑與塔吊荷重表，吊裝前由第三方確認吊具；荷重轉移時以液壓千斤頂讀值與吊索應變計同步記錄，並量測質量塊水平度與各支架卸載量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check each lift's weight and radius against the crane load chart and have rigging verified by a third party; during load transfer, record jack pressures and hanger strain gauges together and measure the block's levelness and the unloading of each frame. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b066-v13-20","title":"高空吊裝與分件組裝：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「分層鋼板吊裝路徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Plate-by-plate lifting route” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若荷重轉移時某支吊索先受力，質量塊會傾斜並在吊點產生超過設計值的局部應力；臨時支架移除順序錯誤也可能造成樓板局部超載與裂縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If one hanger picks up load first during transfer, the block tilts and local stresses at its pick point exceed design values; removing temporary frames in the wrong order can locally overload and crack the slab. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：吊裝期間樓板承受集中荷重，懸吊系統尚未受力，因此需要臨時支架承托質量塊；完成組裝後再逐步把荷重由臨時支架轉移到吊索，這個轉移過程決定了吊索初始張力是否均勻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: During this phase the slab carries concentrated loads while the suspension is not yet loaded, so temporary frames hold the mass; after assembly the load is transferred step by step from the frames to the hangers, and this transfer determines whether the initial hanger tensions are even.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若荷重轉移時某支吊索先受力，質量塊會傾斜並在吊點產生超過設計值的局部應力；臨時支架移除順序錯誤也可能造成樓板局部超載與裂縫。","textEn":"If one hanger picks up load first during transfer, the block tilts and local stresses at its pick point exceed design values; removing temporary frames in the wrong order can locally overload and crack the slab.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高空吊裝與分件組裝」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-level lifting and piece-by-piece assembly\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","若荷重轉移時某支吊索先受力，質量塊會傾斜並在吊點產生超過設計值的局部應力；臨時支架移除順序錯誤也可能造成樓板局部超載與裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","If one hanger picks up load first during transfer, the block tilts and local stresses at its pick point exceed design values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若荷重轉移時某支吊索先受力，質量塊會傾斜並在吊點產生超過設計值的局部應力；臨時支架移除順序錯誤也可能造成樓板局部超載與裂縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If one hanger picks up load first during transfer, the block tilts and local stresses at its pick point exceed design values; removing temporary frames in the wrong order can locally overload and crack the slab. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b066-v13-21","title":"實測頻率與現場調頻：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Measured frequency and on-site tuning: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「現場調頻機構」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “On-site tuning mechanism” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"完工建築的實際頻率常與設計模型相差一到兩成，因為非結構牆、帷幕牆、混凝土實際勁度與質量分布都與假設不同；調諧質量阻尼器的最佳頻帶很窄，所以必須在結構與主要裝修完成後量測實際頻率，再調整擺長、彈簧勁度或附加質量，使阻尼器頻率落在最佳比值附近。調頻設計要預留雙向調整範圍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「現場調頻機構」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The real frequency of a completed building often differs from the design model by ten to twenty percent, because partitions, the façade, actual concrete stiffness and mass distribution differ from the assumptions. A tuned mass damper has a narrow optimum band, so the actual frequency must be measured after the structure and major fit-out are complete, and the pendulum length, spring stiffness or added mass adjusted to place the damper frequency near the optimum ratio. The tuning hardware must allow adjustment in both directions. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “On-site tuning mechanism” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Den Hartog 最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The Den Hartog optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ).","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「現場調頻機構」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “On-site tuning mechanism”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-21-k1","title":"實測頻率與現場調頻","titleEn":"Measured frequency and on-site tuning","text":"完工建築的實際頻率常與設計模型相差一到兩成，因為非結構牆、帷幕牆、混凝土實際勁度與質量分布都與假設不同；調諧質量阻尼器的最佳頻帶很窄，所以必須在結構與主要裝修完成後量測實際頻率，再調整擺長、彈簧勁度或附加質量，使阻尼器頻率落在最佳比值附近。調頻設計要預留雙向調整範圍。","textEn":"The real frequency of a completed building often differs from the design model by ten to twenty percent, because partitions, the façade, actual concrete stiffness and mass distribution differ from the assumptions. A tuned mass damper has a narrow optimum band, so the actual frequency must be measured after the structure and major fit-out are complete, and the pendulum length, spring stiffness or added mass adjusted to place the damper frequency near the optimum ratio.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「實測頻率與現場調頻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measured frequency and on-site tuning\" is correct?","options":["完工建築的實際頻率常與設計模型相差一到兩成，因為非結構牆、帷幕牆、混凝土實際勁度與質量分布都與假設不同。","阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。"],"optionsEn":["The real frequency of a completed building often differs from the design model by ten to twenty percent, because partitions, the façade, actual concrete stiffness and mass distribution differ from the assumptions.","A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption."],"answer":0,"explanation":"完工建築的實際頻率常與設計模型相差一到兩成，因為非結構牆、帷幕牆、混凝土實際勁度與質量分布都與假設不同；調諧質量阻尼器的最佳頻帶很窄，所以必須在結構與主要裝修完成後量測實際頻率，再調整擺長、彈簧勁度或附加質量，使阻尼器頻率落在最佳比值附近。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The real frequency of a completed building often differs from the design model by ten to twenty percent, because partitions, the façade, actual concrete stiffness and mass distribution differ from the assumptions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b066-v13-22","title":"實測頻率與現場調頻：定量估算","titleEn":"Measured frequency and on-site tuning: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「現場調頻機構」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “On-site tuning mechanism” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Den Hartog 最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ)。μ = 0.0066 時 f_opt = 0.9934，結構實測 0.140 Hz 對應阻尼器 0.139 Hz。由 L ∝ 1/f²，頻率要降 5% 時擺長須增加 1/0.95² − 1 ≈ 10.8%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The Den Hartog optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ). For μ = 0.0066, f_opt = 0.9934, so a measured 0.140 Hz building calls for a 0.139 Hz damper. Because L ∝ 1/f², lowering the frequency by 5% needs a length increase of 1/0.95² − 1 ≈ 10.8%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以環境振動量測取得結構實際頻率後，先鎖定擺錘量一次、再釋放擺錘量一次，確認雙峰位置大致對稱；調整後重新做自由衰減或強制振動試驗，記錄最終擺長與頻率比。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After ambient measurement of the actual building frequency, measure once with the pendulum locked and once released, confirming that the two peaks are roughly symmetric; after adjustment repeat a free-decay or forced-vibration test and record the final length and frequency ratio.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Den Hartog 最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ)。μ = 0.0066 時 f_opt = 0.9934，結構實測 0.140 Hz 對應阻尼器 0.139 Hz。由 L ∝ 1/f²，頻率要降 5% 時擺長須增加 1/0.95² − 1 ≈ 10.8%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The Den Hartog optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ). For μ = 0.0066, f_opt = 0.9934, so a measured 0.140 Hz building calls for a 0.139 Hz damper. Because L ∝ 1/f², lowering the frequency by 5% needs a length increase of 1/0.95² − 1 ≈ 10.8%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「實測頻率與現場調頻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measured frequency and on-site tuning\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。","Den Hartog 最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ)。","超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。"],"optionsEn":["A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.","The Den Hartog optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ).","Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Den Hartog 最佳頻率比 f_opt = 1/(1+μ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The Den Hartog optimum frequency ratio is f_opt = 1/(1+μ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b066-v13-23","title":"實測頻率與現場調頻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Measured frequency and on-site tuning: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「現場調頻機構」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “On-site tuning mechanism” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以環境振動量測取得結構實際頻率後，先鎖定擺錘量一次、再釋放擺錘量一次，確認雙峰位置大致對稱；調整後重新做自由衰減或強制振動試驗，記錄最終擺長與頻率比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After ambient measurement of the actual building frequency, measure once with the pendulum locked and once released, confirming that the two peaks are roughly symmetric; after adjustment repeat a free-decay or forced-vibration test and record the final length and frequency ratio. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把調頻機構（可調吊點、加減配重或彈簧）納入設計與合約範圍，並安排在帷幕牆與主要機電完成後的固定時程進行調頻驗收，必要時一年後再複核一次。","observationEn":"Site practice: Include the tuning hardware (adjustable pick points, removable weights or springs) in the design and contract, schedule tuning acceptance after the façade and major services are complete, and re-check after about a year if needed.","failure":"注意干擾：若以設計頻率直接製造而不預留調整，實際頻率偏離 5% 時，雙自由度模型顯示等效阻尼可能由約 3.7% 降到約 2.1%，加速度改善幅度明顯縮水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Building to the design frequency without adjustment range means that a 5% offset in the actual frequency can drop the equivalent damping in the two-degree-of-freedom model from about 3.7% to about 2.1%, sharply shrinking the acceleration benefit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以環境振動量測取得結構實際頻率後，先鎖定擺錘量一次、再釋放擺錘量一次，確認雙峰位置大致對稱；調整後重新做自由衰減或強制振動試驗，記錄最終擺長與頻率比。","textEn":"After ambient measurement of the actual building frequency, measure once with the pendulum locked and once released, confirming that the two peaks are roughly symmetric; after adjustment repeat a free-decay or forced-vibration test and record the final length and frequency ratio.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把調頻機構（可調吊點、加減配重或彈簧）納入設計與合約範圍，並安排在帷幕牆與主要機電完成後的固定時程進行調頻驗收，必要時一年後再複核一次。","textEn":"Include the tuning hardware (adjustable pick points, removable weights or springs) in the design and contract, schedule tuning acceptance after the façade and major services are complete, and re-check after about a year if needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「實測頻率與現場調頻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measured frequency and on-site tuning\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。","以環境振動量測取得結構實際頻率後，先鎖定擺錘量一次、再釋放擺錘量一次，確認雙峰位置大致對稱；調整後重新做自由衰減或強制振動試驗，記錄最終擺長與頻率比。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.","After ambient measurement of the actual building frequency, measure once with the pendulum locked and once released, confirming that the two peaks are roughly symmetric."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以環境振動量測取得結構實際頻率後，先鎖定擺錘量一次、再釋放擺錘量一次，確認雙峰位置大致對稱；調整後重新做自由衰減或強制振動試驗，記錄最終擺長與頻率比。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After ambient measurement of the actual building frequency, measure once with the pendulum locked and once released, confirming that the two peaks are roughly symmetric; after adjustment repeat a free-decay or forced-vibration test and record the final length and frequency ratio. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b066-v13-24","title":"實測頻率與現場調頻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measured frequency and on-site tuning: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「現場調頻機構」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “On-site tuning mechanism” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若以設計頻率直接製造而不預留調整，實際頻率偏離 5% 時，雙自由度模型顯示等效阻尼可能由約 3.7% 降到約 2.1%，加速度改善幅度明顯縮水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Building to the design frequency without adjustment range means that a 5% offset in the actual frequency can drop the equivalent damping in the two-degree-of-freedom model from about 3.7% to about 2.1%, sharply shrinking the acceleration benefit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：調頻設計要預留雙向調整範圍。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The tuning hardware must allow adjustment in both directions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若以設計頻率直接製造而不預留調整，實際頻率偏離 5% 時，雙自由度模型顯示等效阻尼可能由約 3.7% 降到約 2.1%，加速度改善幅度明顯縮水。","textEn":"Building to the design frequency without adjustment range means that a 5% offset in the actual frequency can drop the equivalent damping in the two-degree-of-freedom model from about 3.7% to about 2.1%, sharply shrinking the acceleration benefit.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實測頻率與現場調頻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measured frequency and on-site tuning\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若以設計頻率直接製造而不預留調整，實際頻率偏離 5% 時，雙自由度模型顯示等效阻尼可能由約 3.7% 降到約 2.1%，加速度改善幅度明顯縮水。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。"],"optionsEn":["Building to the design frequency without adjustment range means that a 5% offset in the actual frequency can drop the equivalent damping in the two-degree-of-freedom model from about 3.7% to about 2.1%, sharply shrinking the acceleration benefit.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若以設計頻率直接製造而不預留調整，實際頻率偏離 5% 時，雙自由度模型顯示等效阻尼可能由約 3.7% 降到約 2.1%，加速度改善幅度明顯縮水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Building to the design frequency without adjustment range means that a 5% offset in the actual frequency can drop the equivalent damping in the two-degree-of-freedom model from about 3.7% to about 2.1%, sharply shrinking the acceleration benefit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b066-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「環境振動量測與系統識別」與「阻尼器整體性能驗證」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification\" and \"Whole-system damper performance verification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b066-v13-25","title":"環境振動量測與系統識別：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「頂層加速度計陣列」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Top-level accelerometer array” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"高樓在日常風與交通擾動下一直有微小振動，只要在頂部與阻尼器上放置高靈敏度加速度計長時間記錄，就能用頻域分解或峰值挑選法辨識模態頻率、振型與阻尼比。量測要同時涵蓋兩個水平方向與扭轉（至少兩個角落），並同步記錄風速風向，才能把阻尼比與振幅、風況關聯起來；超高層阻尼比往往隨振幅改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「頂層加速度計陣列」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A tall building vibrates slightly all the time under everyday wind and traffic, so long records from sensitive accelerometers at the top and on the damper let engineers identify modal frequencies, shapes and damping ratios by frequency-domain decomposition or peak picking. Measurements must cover both horizontal directions and torsion (at least two corners) and be synchronised with wind speed and direction, so that damping can be related to amplitude and wind condition; damping in supertall towers often changes with amplitude. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Top-level accelerometer array” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：半功率頻寬法 ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The half-power bandwidth method gives ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「頂層加速度計陣列」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Top-level accelerometer array”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-25-k1","title":"環境振動量測與系統識別","titleEn":"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification","text":"高樓在日常風與交通擾動下一直有微小振動，只要在頂部與阻尼器上放置高靈敏度加速度計長時間記錄，就能用頻域分解或峰值挑選法辨識模態頻率、振型與阻尼比。量測要同時涵蓋兩個水平方向與扭轉（至少兩個角落），並同步記錄風速風向，才能把阻尼比與振幅、風況關聯起來；超高層阻尼比往往隨振幅改變。","textEn":"A tall building vibrates slightly all the time under everyday wind and traffic, so long records from sensitive accelerometers at the top and on the damper let engineers identify modal frequencies, shapes and damping ratios by frequency-domain decomposition or peak picking. Measurements must cover both horizontal directions and torsion (at least two corners) and be synchronised with wind speed and direction, so that damping can be related to amplitude and wind condition; damping in supertall towers often changes with amplitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環境振動量測與系統識別」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification\" is correct?","options":["只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。","高樓在日常風與交通擾動下一直有微小振動，只要在頂部與阻尼器上放置高靈敏度加速度計長時間記錄，就能用頻域分解或峰值挑選法辨識模態頻率、振型與阻尼比。","阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。"],"optionsEn":["Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption.","A tall building vibrates slightly all the time under everyday wind and traffic, so long records from sensitive accelerometers at the top and on the damper let engineers identify modal frequencies, shapes and damping ratios by frequency-domain decomposition or peak picking.","Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高樓在日常風與交通擾動下一直有微小振動，只要在頂部與阻尼器上放置高靈敏度加速度計長時間記錄，就能用頻域分解或峰值挑選法辨識模態頻率、振型與阻尼比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A tall building vibrates slightly all the time under everyday wind and traffic, so long records from sensitive accelerometers at the top and on the damper let engineers identify modal frequencies, shapes and damping ratios by frequency-domain decomposition or peak picking. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b066-v13-26","title":"環境振動量測與系統識別：定量估算","titleEn":"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「頂層加速度計陣列」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Top-level accelerometer array” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：半功率頻寬法 ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)。若共振峰 f_n = 0.140 Hz，半功率點 f₁ = 0.1383 Hz、f₂ = 0.1418 Hz，則 ζ ≈ 0.0035/0.280 ≈ 1.25%；頻率解析度需優於 0.0005 Hz，記錄長度至少約 1/0.0005 = 2,000 s。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The half-power bandwidth method gives ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n). With a peak at f_n = 0.140 Hz and half-power points at f₁ = 0.1383 Hz and f₂ = 0.1418 Hz, ζ ≈ 0.0035/0.280 ≈ 1.25%; resolving 0.0005 Hz needs a record of at least about 1/0.0005 = 2,000 s. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較兩種辨識方法（例如頻域分解與隨機子空間法）得到的頻率與阻尼，差異應在可解釋範圍內；感測器先在地面並排做相互比對，記錄方位與安裝位置照片，並把結果與有限元素模態比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare frequencies and damping from two identification methods, such as frequency-domain decomposition and stochastic subspace identification, and require explainable agreement; co-locate sensors on the ground first for a huddle test, record orientations and mounting photographs, and compare results with finite-element modes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"半功率頻寬法 ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)。若共振峰 f_n = 0.140 Hz，半功率點 f₁ = 0.1383 Hz、f₂ = 0.1418 Hz，則 ζ ≈ 0.0035/0.280 ≈ 1.25%；頻率解析度需優於 0.0005 Hz，記錄長度至少約 1/0.0005 = 2,000 s。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The half-power bandwidth method gives ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n). With a peak at f_n = 0.140 Hz and half-power points at f₁ = 0.1383 Hz and f₂ = 0.1418 Hz, ζ ≈ 0.0035/0.280 ≈ 1.25%; resolving 0.0005 Hz needs a record of at least about 1/0.0005 = 2,000 s. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環境振動量測與系統識別」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。","阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。","半功率頻寬法 ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)。"],"optionsEn":["A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring.","A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight.","The half-power bandwidth method gives ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"半功率頻寬法 ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The half-power bandwidth method gives ζ ≈ (f₂ − f₁)/(2f_n). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b066-v13-27","title":"環境振動量測與系統識別：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「頂層加速度計陣列」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Top-level accelerometer array” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較兩種辨識方法（例如頻域分解與隨機子空間法）得到的頻率與阻尼，差異應在可解釋範圍內；感測器先在地面並排做相互比對，記錄方位與安裝位置照片，並把結果與有限元素模態比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare frequencies and damping from two identification methods, such as frequency-domain decomposition and stochastic subspace identification, and require explainable agreement; co-locate sensors on the ground first for a huddle test, record orientations and mounting photographs, and compare results with finite-element modes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測系統應包含時間同步、遠端資料傳輸與資料品質檢查（缺值、飽和、漂移），量測報告需附原始資料格式與處理參數，方便日後由他人重算。","observationEn":"Site practice: The monitoring system should include time synchronisation, remote data transfer and data-quality checks (gaps, saturation, drift), and the report should attach the raw data format and processing parameters so others can recompute later.","failure":"注意干擾：記錄太短或頻率解析度不足時，半功率頻寬被放大，算出的阻尼比偏高，讓人誤以為阻尼器表現良好；感測器方向裝反則會把兩個方向的模態混在一起。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Records that are too short or too coarse in frequency inflate the half-power bandwidth and overstate damping, suggesting the damper performs better than it does; a reversed sensor orientation mixes the modes of the two directions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較兩種辨識方法（例如頻域分解與隨機子空間法）得到的頻率與阻尼，差異應在可解釋範圍內；感測器先在地面並排做相互比對，記錄方位與安裝位置照片，並把結果與有限元素模態比較。","textEn":"Compare frequencies and damping from two identification methods, such as frequency-domain decomposition and stochastic subspace identification, and require explainable agreement; co-locate sensors on the ground first for a huddle test, record orientations and mounting photographs, and compare results with finite-element modes.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測系統應包含時間同步、遠端資料傳輸與資料品質檢查（缺值、飽和、漂移），量測報告需附原始資料格式與處理參數，方便日後由他人重算。","textEn":"The monitoring system should include time synchronisation, remote data transfer and data-quality checks (gaps, saturation, drift), and the report should attach the raw data format and processing parameters so others can recompute later.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環境振動量測與系統識別」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification\"?","options":["比較兩種辨識方法（例如頻域分解與隨機子空間法）得到的頻率與阻尼，差異應在可解釋範圍內。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Compare frequencies and damping from two identification methods, such as frequency-domain decomposition and stochastic subspace identification, and require explainable agreement.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較兩種辨識方法（例如頻域分解與隨機子空間法）得到的頻率與阻尼，差異應在可解釋範圍內；感測器先在地面並排做相互比對，記錄方位與安裝位置照片，並把結果與有限元素模態比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare frequencies and damping from two identification methods, such as frequency-domain decomposition and stochastic subspace identification, and require explainable agreement; co-locate sensors on the ground first for a huddle test, record orientations and mounting photographs, and compare results with finite-element modes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b066-v13-28","title":"環境振動量測與系統識別：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「頂層加速度計陣列」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Top-level accelerometer array” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"記錄太短或頻率解析度不足時，半功率頻寬被放大，算出的阻尼比偏高，讓人誤以為阻尼器表現良好；感測器方向裝反則會把兩個方向的模態混在一起。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Records that are too short or too coarse in frequency inflate the half-power bandwidth and overstate damping, suggesting the damper performs better than it does; a reversed sensor orientation mixes the modes of the two directions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：量測要同時涵蓋兩個水平方向與扭轉（至少兩個角落），並同步記錄風速風向，才能把阻尼比與振幅、風況關聯起來；超高層阻尼比往往隨振幅改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measurements must cover both horizontal directions and torsion (at least two corners) and be synchronised with wind speed and direction, so that damping can be related to amplitude and wind condition; damping in supertall towers often changes with amplitude.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"記錄太短或頻率解析度不足時，半功率頻寬被放大，算出的阻尼比偏高，讓人誤以為阻尼器表現良好；感測器方向裝反則會把兩個方向的模態混在一起。","textEn":"Records that are too short or too coarse in frequency inflate the half-power bandwidth and overstate damping, suggesting the damper performs better than it does; a reversed sensor orientation mixes the modes of the two directions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環境振動量測與系統識別」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ambient vibration measurement and system identification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","記錄太短或頻率解析度不足時，半功率頻寬被放大，算出的阻尼比偏高，讓人誤以為阻尼器表現良好；感測器方向裝反則會把兩個方向的模態混在一起。","阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Records that are too short or too coarse in frequency inflate the half-power bandwidth and overstate damping, suggesting the damper performs better than it does.","Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building."],"answer":1,"explanation":"記錄太短或頻率解析度不足時，半功率頻寬被放大，算出的阻尼比偏高，讓人誤以為阻尼器表現良好；感測器方向裝反則會把兩個方向的模態混在一起。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Records that are too short or too coarse in frequency inflate the half-power bandwidth and overstate damping, suggesting the damper performs better than it does; a reversed sensor orientation mixes the modes of the two directions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b066-v13-29","title":"阻尼器整體性能驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Whole-system damper performance verification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"零件試驗合格不代表裝在樓上的整套系統合格，因此完工後要做系統級驗證：可用千斤頂或纜線把擺錘拉離平衡位置後釋放，觀察擺錘與結構的自由衰減；也可用阻尼器自身或附加的作動器做強制振動掃頻。藉由比較鎖定與釋放擺錘時結構的衰減率或頻率響應，直接得到阻尼器提供的附加阻尼。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Passing component tests does not prove the installed system, so after completion a system-level verification is done: pull the pendulum off equilibrium with jacks or cables and release it to observe the free decay of the pendulum and structure, or use the damper itself or an added actuator for a forced-vibration sweep. Comparing structural decay or frequency response with the pendulum locked and released gives the added damping directly. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ)，ζ ≈ δ/(2π)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The logarithmic decrement is δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ) with ζ ≈ δ/(2π).","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-29-k1","title":"阻尼器整體性能驗證","titleEn":"Whole-system damper performance verification","text":"零件試驗合格不代表裝在樓上的整套系統合格，因此完工後要做系統級驗證：可用千斤頂或纜線把擺錘拉離平衡位置後釋放，觀察擺錘與結構的自由衰減；也可用阻尼器自身或附加的作動器做強制振動掃頻。藉由比較鎖定與釋放擺錘時結構的衰減率或頻率響應，直接得到阻尼器提供的附加阻尼。","textEn":"Passing component tests does not prove the installed system, so after completion a system-level verification is done: pull the pendulum off equilibrium with jacks or cables and release it to observe the free decay of the pendulum and structure, or use the damper itself or an added actuator for a forced-vibration sweep. Comparing structural decay or frequency response with the pendulum locked and released gives the added damping directly.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻尼器整體性能驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Whole-system damper performance verification\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。","阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。","零件試驗合格不代表裝在樓上的整套系統合格，因此完工後要做系統級驗證：可用千斤頂或纜線把擺錘拉離平衡位置後釋放，觀察擺錘與結構的自由衰減。"],"optionsEn":["Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building.","A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.","Passing component tests does not prove the installed system, so after completion a system-level verification is done: pull the pendulum off equilibrium with jacks or cables and release it to observe the free decay of the pendulum and structure, or use the damper itself or an added actuator for a forced-vibration sweep."],"answer":2,"explanation":"零件試驗合格不代表裝在樓上的整套系統合格，因此完工後要做系統級驗證：可用千斤頂或纜線把擺錘拉離平衡位置後釋放，觀察擺錘與結構的自由衰減；也可用阻尼器自身或附加的作動器做強制振動掃頻。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Passing component tests does not prove the installed system, so after completion a system-level verification is done: pull the pendulum off equilibrium with jacks or cables and release it to observe the free decay of the pendulum and structure, or use the damper itself or an added actuator for a forced-vibration sweep. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b066-v13-30","title":"阻尼器整體性能驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Whole-system damper performance verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ)，ζ ≈ δ/(2π)。若振幅由 100 mm 經 10 個週期降為 53 mm，δ = ln(100/53)/10 = 0.0635，ζ ≈ 1.0%；釋放擺錘後若 10 個週期降為 10 mm，δ = 0.230，ζ ≈ 3.7%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The logarithmic decrement is δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ) with ζ ≈ δ/(2π). If amplitude falls from 100 mm to 53 mm in 10 cycles, δ = ln(100/53)/10 = 0.0635 and ζ ≈ 1.0%; if, with the pendulum released, it falls to 10 mm in 10 cycles, δ = 0.230 and ζ ≈ 3.7%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：事先寫好試驗計畫：初始拉離量、釋放方式、量測點、取樣率、允收準則（例如附加阻尼不低於設計值的 80%），並重複三次取平均；試驗時段選在低風速時，同步記錄風速以排除外力干擾。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Write the test plan beforehand: initial offset, release method, measurement points, sampling rate and acceptance criterion (for example added damping not below 80% of the design value), and repeat three times for an average; test in low wind and record wind speed simultaneously to exclude external forcing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ)，ζ ≈ δ/(2π)。若振幅由 100 mm 經 10 個週期降為 53 mm，δ = ln(100/53)/10 = 0.0635，ζ ≈ 1.0%；釋放擺錘後若 10 個週期降為 10 mm，δ = 0.230，ζ ≈ 3.7%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The logarithmic decrement is δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ) with ζ ≈ δ/(2π). If amplitude falls from 100 mm to 53 mm in 10 cycles, δ = ln(100/53)/10 = 0.0635 and ζ ≈ 1.0%; if, with the pendulum released, it falls to 10 mm in 10 cycles, δ = 0.230 and ζ ≈ 3.7%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「阻尼器整體性能驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Whole-system damper performance verification\", which statement holds?","options":["對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ)，ζ ≈ δ/(2π)。","超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。","質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。"],"optionsEn":["The logarithmic decrement is δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ) with ζ ≈ δ/(2π).","Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened.","The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ)，ζ ≈ δ/(2π)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The logarithmic decrement is δ = (1/n)·ln(x₀/xₙ) with ζ ≈ δ/(2π). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b066-v13-31","title":"阻尼器整體性能驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Whole-system damper performance verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"事先寫好試驗計畫：初始拉離量、釋放方式、量測點、取樣率、允收準則（例如附加阻尼不低於設計值的 80%），並重複三次取平均；試驗時段選在低風速時，同步記錄風速以排除外力干擾。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Write the test plan beforehand: initial offset, release method, measurement points, sampling rate and acceptance criterion (for example added damping not below 80% of the design value), and repeat three times for an average; test in low wind and record wind speed simultaneously to exclude external forcing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：系統試驗報告要記錄擺長、配重、阻尼器編號與溫度，作為之後每次維護後比對的基準；試驗前須確認行程限制器與安全鎖定可靠，並劃定人員禁入區。","observationEn":"Site practice: The system test report should record pendulum length, weights, damper serial numbers and temperature as the baseline for every later maintenance comparison; before testing confirm stroke limiters and safety locks, and mark exclusion zones for personnel.","failure":"注意干擾：若在強風下做自由衰減，外力持續輸入會讓衰減曲線失真；擺錘若碰到緩衝器或導軌摩擦突然改變，衰減曲線會出現轉折，用單一 ζ 擬合就會得到錯誤結論。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Free decay in strong wind is distorted by continued forcing; if the pendulum touches a bumper or guide friction changes abruptly, the decay curve kinks, and fitting a single ζ gives the wrong conclusion. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"事先寫好試驗計畫：初始拉離量、釋放方式、量測點、取樣率、允收準則（例如附加阻尼不低於設計值的 80%），並重複三次取平均；試驗時段選在低風速時，同步記錄風速以排除外力干擾。","textEn":"Write the test plan beforehand: initial offset, release method, measurement points, sampling rate and acceptance criterion (for example added damping not below 80% of the design value), and repeat three times for an average; test in low wind and record wind speed simultaneously to exclude external forcing.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"系統試驗報告要記錄擺長、配重、阻尼器編號與溫度，作為之後每次維護後比對的基準；試驗前須確認行程限制器與安全鎖定可靠，並劃定人員禁入區。","textEn":"The system test report should record pendulum length, weights, damper serial numbers and temperature as the baseline for every later maintenance comparison; before testing confirm stroke limiters and safety locks, and mark exclusion zones for personnel.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「阻尼器整體性能驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Whole-system damper performance verification\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","事先寫好試驗計畫：初始拉離量、釋放方式、量測點、取樣率、允收準則（例如附加阻尼不低於設計值的 80%），並重複三次取平均。","質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Write the test plan beforehand: initial offset, release method, measurement points, sampling rate and acceptance criterion (for example added damping not below 80% of the design value), and repeat three times for an average.","Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan."],"answer":1,"explanation":"事先寫好試驗計畫：初始拉離量、釋放方式、量測點、取樣率、允收準則（例如附加阻尼不低於設計值的 80%），並重複三次取平均；試驗時段選在低風速時，同步記錄風速以排除外力干擾。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Write the test plan beforehand: initial offset, release method, measurement points, sampling rate and acceptance criterion (for example added damping not below 80% of the design value), and repeat three times for an average; test in low wind and record wind speed simultaneously to exclude external forcing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b066-v13-32","title":"阻尼器整體性能驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Whole-system damper performance verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自由衰減與強制振動試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free-decay and forced-vibration tests” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在強風下做自由衰減，外力持續輸入會讓衰減曲線失真；擺錘若碰到緩衝器或導軌摩擦突然改變，衰減曲線會出現轉折，用單一 ζ 擬合就會得到錯誤結論。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Free decay in strong wind is distorted by continued forcing; if the pendulum touches a bumper or guide friction changes abruptly, the decay curve kinks, and fitting a single ζ gives the wrong conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：藉由比較鎖定與釋放擺錘時結構的衰減率或頻率響應，直接得到阻尼器提供的附加阻尼。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Comparing structural decay or frequency response with the pendulum locked and released gives the added damping directly.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器零件出廠試驗合格，就能證明整棟樓的減振性能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Factory tests of the damper components prove the vibration performance of the whole building.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在強風下做自由衰減，外力持續輸入會讓衰減曲線失真；擺錘若碰到緩衝器或導軌摩擦突然改變，衰減曲線會出現轉折，用單一 ζ 擬合就會得到錯誤結論。","textEn":"Free decay in strong wind is distorted by continued forcing; if the pendulum touches a bumper or guide friction changes abruptly, the decay curve kinks, and fitting a single ζ gives the wrong conclusion.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻尼器整體性能驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Whole-system damper performance verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。","若在強風下做自由衰減，外力持續輸入會讓衰減曲線失真；擺錘若碰到緩衝器或導軌摩擦突然改變，衰減曲線會出現轉折，用單一 ζ 擬合就會得到錯誤結論。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.","Free decay in strong wind is distorted by continued forcing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若在強風下做自由衰減，外力持續輸入會讓衰減曲線失真；擺錘若碰到緩衝器或導軌摩擦突然改變，衰減曲線會出現轉折，用單一 ζ 擬合就會得到錯誤結論。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Free decay in strong wind is distorted by continued forcing; if the pendulum touches a bumper or guide friction changes abruptly, the decay curve kinks, and fitting a single ζ gives the wrong conclusion. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b066-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「極端事件的行程限制與防撞」與「長期性能、維護與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events\" and \"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b066-v13-33","title":"極端事件的行程限制與防撞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「緩衝環與行程限制器」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Snubber ring and stroke limiters” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"颱風或地震時，擺錘相對位移可能遠大於日常值；若不限制，質量塊會撞到結構或機電設備。因此大型阻尼器設有緩衝環、油壓緩衝器或非線性彈簧，在超過設計行程時逐漸吸收動能，把衝擊力分散到結構可承受的範圍。行程限制的設計是在減振效果與安全之間取捨：限制太早會削弱效果，太晚則衝擊力過大。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「緩衝環與行程限制器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a typhoon or earthquake the pendulum's relative displacement can far exceed everyday values; without limits the mass would hit the structure or services. Large dampers therefore have snubber rings, hydraulic buffers or nonlinear springs that progressively absorb kinetic energy beyond the design stroke, spreading the impact force to levels the structure can take. Stroke limiting trades vibration reduction against safety: limiting too early weakens performance, too late creates excessive impact force. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Snubber ring and stroke limiters” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：擺錘以 0.6 m/s 撞到緩衝器時動能 E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ；若緩衝行程 0.3 m 且力量近似線性增加，峰值力 F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If the pendulum reaches the buffer at 0.6 m/s, its kinetic energy is E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ; with 0.3 m of buffer travel and a roughly linear force rise, the peak force is F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「緩衝環與行程限制器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Snubber ring and stroke limiters”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-33-k1","title":"極端事件的行程限制與防撞","titleEn":"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events","text":"颱風或地震時，擺錘相對位移可能遠大於日常值；若不限制，質量塊會撞到結構或機電設備。因此大型阻尼器設有緩衝環、油壓緩衝器或非線性彈簧，在超過設計行程時逐漸吸收動能，把衝擊力分散到結構可承受的範圍。","textEn":"In a typhoon or earthquake the pendulum's relative displacement can far exceed everyday values; without limits the mass would hit the structure or services. Large dampers therefore have snubber rings, hydraulic buffers or nonlinear springs that progressively absorb kinetic energy beyond the design stroke, spreading the impact force to levels the structure can take.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「極端事件的行程限制與防撞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events\" is correct?","options":["颱風或地震時，擺錘相對位移可能遠大於日常值；若不限制，質量塊會撞到結構或機電設備。","阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。","阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。"],"optionsEn":["In a typhoon or earthquake the pendulum's relative displacement can far exceed everyday values; without limits the mass would hit the structure or services.","A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.","A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"颱風或地震時，擺錘相對位移可能遠大於日常值；若不限制，質量塊會撞到結構或機電設備。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a typhoon or earthquake the pendulum's relative displacement can far exceed everyday values; without limits the mass would hit the structure or services. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b066-v13-34","title":"極端事件的行程限制與防撞：定量估算","titleEn":"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「緩衝環與行程限制器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Snubber ring and stroke limiters” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：擺錘以 0.6 m/s 撞到緩衝器時動能 E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ；若緩衝行程 0.3 m 且力量近似線性增加，峰值力 F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If the pendulum reaches the buffer at 0.6 m/s, its kinetic energy is E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ; with 0.3 m of buffer travel and a roughly linear force rise, the peak force is F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以非線性時間歷程分析輸入設計颱風與地震紀錄，檢查擺錘最大位移、接觸次數與緩衝力，並確認支撐緩衝器的樓板與構件強度；完工後確認實際淨距與緩衝器預壓符合圖說。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run nonlinear time-history analyses with design typhoon and earthquake records to check maximum pendulum displacement, contact count and buffer forces, and verify the slab and members supporting the buffers; after completion confirm actual clearances and buffer preload against the drawings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"擺錘以 0.6 m/s 撞到緩衝器時動能 E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ；若緩衝行程 0.3 m 且力量近似線性增加，峰值力 F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If the pendulum reaches the buffer at 0.6 m/s, its kinetic energy is E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ; with 0.3 m of buffer travel and a roughly linear force rise, the peak force is F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「極端事件的行程限制與防撞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器的效果只取決於它佔整棟樓總重的百分比。","擺錘以 0.6 m/s 撞到緩衝器時動能 E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ。","阻尼器的阻尼係數越大，減振效果一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["A damper's effect depends only on its percentage of the total building weight.","If the pendulum reaches the buffer at 0.6 m/s, its kinetic energy is E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ.","The larger the damping coefficient, the better the vibration reduction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擺錘以 0.6 m/s 撞到緩衝器時動能 E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ；若緩衝行程 0.3 m 且力量近似線性增加，峰值力 F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If the pendulum reaches the buffer at 0.6 m/s, its kinetic energy is E = ½·m·v² = 0.5×660,000×0.6² ≈ 119 kJ; with 0.3 m of buffer travel and a roughly linear force rise, the peak force is F = 2E/s = 2×119,000/0.3 ≈ 790 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b066-v13-35","title":"極端事件的行程限制與防撞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「緩衝環與行程限制器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Snubber ring and stroke limiters” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入設計颱風與地震紀錄，檢查擺錘最大位移、接觸次數與緩衝力，並確認支撐緩衝器的樓板與構件強度；完工後確認實際淨距與緩衝器預壓符合圖說。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with design typhoon and earthquake records to check maximum pendulum displacement, contact count and buffer forces, and verify the slab and members supporting the buffers; after completion confirm actual clearances and buffer preload against the drawings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：事件後檢查清單應包含緩衝器接觸痕跡、吊索與吊點、阻尼器漏油、擺錘水平度與鎖定裝置，並與事件時的監測資料比對，確認是否需要重新調頻或更換元件。","observationEn":"Site practice: A post-event checklist should cover buffer contact marks, hangers and pick points, damper leaks, block levelness and locking devices, compared with the monitoring data from the event to decide whether retuning or component replacement is needed.","failure":"注意干擾：緩衝器設計不足時，極端事件中質量塊反覆撞擊會損壞阻尼器、吊索與周邊樓板；若擺錘在地震中與結構不同步大幅擺動，也可能對主結構造成不利的附加力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Undersized buffers let the mass impact repeatedly in an extreme event, damaging the dampers, hangers and surrounding slab; if the pendulum swings out of sync during an earthquake it can also apply unfavourable additional forces to the main structure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入設計颱風與地震紀錄，檢查擺錘最大位移、接觸次數與緩衝力，並確認支撐緩衝器的樓板與構件強度；完工後確認實際淨距與緩衝器預壓符合圖說。","textEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with design typhoon and earthquake records to check maximum pendulum displacement, contact count and buffer forces, and verify the slab and members supporting the buffers; after completion confirm actual clearances and buffer preload against the drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"事件後檢查清單應包含緩衝器接觸痕跡、吊索與吊點、阻尼器漏油、擺錘水平度與鎖定裝置，並與事件時的監測資料比對，確認是否需要重新調頻或更換元件。","textEn":"A post-event checklist should cover buffer contact marks, hangers and pick points, damper leaks, block levelness and locking devices, compared with the monitoring data from the event to decide whether retuning or component replacement is needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「極端事件的行程限制與防撞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","阻尼器在工廠依設計頻率調好，到現場就不需要再調整。","以非線性時間歷程分析輸入設計颱風與地震紀錄，檢查擺錘最大位移、接觸次數與緩衝力，並確認支撐緩衝器的樓板與構件強度；完工後確認實際淨距與緩衝器預壓符合圖說。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A damper tuned at the factory to the design frequency needs no adjustment on site.","Run nonlinear time-history analyses with design typhoon and earthquake records to check maximum pendulum displacement, contact count and buffer forces, and verify the slab and members supporting the buffers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以非線性時間歷程分析輸入設計颱風與地震紀錄，檢查擺錘最大位移、接觸次數與緩衝力，並確認支撐緩衝器的樓板與構件強度；完工後確認實際淨距與緩衝器預壓符合圖說。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run nonlinear time-history analyses with design typhoon and earthquake records to check maximum pendulum displacement, contact count and buffer forces, and verify the slab and members supporting the buffers; after completion confirm actual clearances and buffer preload against the drawings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b066-v13-36","title":"極端事件的行程限制與防撞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「緩衝環與行程限制器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Snubber ring and stroke limiters” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"緩衝器設計不足時，極端事件中質量塊反覆撞擊會損壞阻尼器、吊索與周邊樓板；若擺錘在地震中與結構不同步大幅擺動，也可能對主結構造成不利的附加力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Undersized buffers let the mass impact repeatedly in an extreme event, damaging the dampers, hangers and surrounding slab; if the pendulum swings out of sync during an earthquake it can also apply unfavourable additional forces to the main structure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：行程限制的設計是在減振效果與安全之間取捨：限制太早會削弱效果，太晚則衝擊力過大。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stroke limiting trades vibration reduction against safety: limiting too early weakens performance, too late creates excessive impact force.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器在地震中一定能像在風中一樣大幅降低結構反應。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tuned mass damper always reduces earthquake response as effectively as wind response.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"緩衝器設計不足時，極端事件中質量塊反覆撞擊會損壞阻尼器、吊索與周邊樓板；若擺錘在地震中與結構不同步大幅擺動，也可能對主結構造成不利的附加力。","textEn":"Undersized buffers let the mass impact repeatedly in an extreme event, damaging the dampers, hangers and surrounding slab; if the pendulum swings out of sync during an earthquake it can also apply unfavourable additional forces to the main structure.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「極端事件的行程限制與防撞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stroke limits and impact protection in extreme events\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["緩衝器設計不足時，極端事件中質量塊反覆撞擊會損壞阻尼器、吊索與周邊樓板；若擺錘在地震中與結構不同步大幅擺動，也可能對主結構造成不利的附加力。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。"],"optionsEn":["Undersized buffers let the mass impact repeatedly in an extreme event, damaging the dampers, hangers and surrounding slab.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring."],"answer":0,"explanation":"緩衝器設計不足時，極端事件中質量塊反覆撞擊會損壞阻尼器、吊索與周邊樓板；若擺錘在地震中與結構不同步大幅擺動，也可能對主結構造成不利的附加力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Undersized buffers let the mass impact repeatedly in an extreme event, damaging the dampers, hangers and surrounding slab; if the pendulum swings out of sync during an earthquake it can also apply unfavourable additional forces to the main structure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b066-v13-37","title":"長期性能、維護與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「監測與維護紀錄」如何影響高層建築調諧質量阻尼器的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Monitoring and maintenance records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Tuned mass dampers for tall buildings”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"阻尼器設計壽命常與建築相同，但其性能會隨結構頻率改變、阻尼液老化、吊索鬆弛與溫度而漂移；建築改裝增加或移除大量質量，也會讓原本的調頻失準。因此交接文件必須包含設計參數、調頻紀錄、試驗基準、檢查週期與允收範圍，並把長期監測資料定期與基準比對，偏離時啟動重新調頻或維修。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「監測與維護紀錄」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A damper's design life often matches the building's, yet its performance drifts with changes in structural frequency, fluid ageing, hanger slack and temperature; renovations that add or remove large masses can also detune it. Handover documents must therefore contain design parameters, tuning records, test baselines, inspection intervals and acceptance ranges, and long-term monitoring data must be compared with the baseline periodically to trigger retuning or repair when they diverge. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Monitoring and maintenance records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 μ = 0.0066、結構阻尼 1% 的雙自由度模型計算，最佳調頻時共振放大係數由 50 降到約 13.6（等效阻尼約 3.7%）；頻率比偏離 ±5% 時放大係數回升到約 23，等效阻尼約 2.1%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: In a two-degree-of-freedom model with μ = 0.0066 and 1% structural damping, optimum tuning lowers the resonant amplification from 50 to about 13.6 (equivalent damping about 3.7%); a ±5% frequency-ratio offset raises it back to about 23, an equivalent damping of about 2.1%.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「監測與維護紀錄」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Monitoring and maintenance records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-37-k1","title":"長期性能、維護與交接","titleEn":"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover","text":"阻尼器設計壽命常與建築相同，但其性能會隨結構頻率改變、阻尼液老化、吊索鬆弛與溫度而漂移；建築改裝增加或移除大量質量，也會讓原本的調頻失準。因此交接文件必須包含設計參數、調頻紀錄、試驗基準、檢查週期與允收範圍，並把長期監測資料定期與基準比對，偏離時啟動重新調頻或維修。","textEn":"A damper's design life often matches the building's, yet its performance drifts with changes in structural frequency, fluid ageing, hanger slack and temperature; renovations that add or remove large masses can also detune it. Handover documents must therefore contain design parameters, tuning records, test baselines, inspection intervals and acceptance ranges, and long-term monitoring data must be compared with the baseline periodically to trigger retuning or repair when they diverge.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長期性能、維護與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。","阻尼器設計壽命常與建築相同，但其性能會隨結構頻率改變、阻尼液老化、吊索鬆弛與溫度而漂移；建築改裝增加或移除大量質量，也會讓原本的調頻失準。","超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。"],"optionsEn":["A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring.","A damper's design life often matches the building's, yet its performance drifts with changes in structural frequency, fluid ageing, hanger slack and temperature.","Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened."],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻尼器設計壽命常與建築相同，但其性能會隨結構頻率改變、阻尼液老化、吊索鬆弛與溫度而漂移；建築改裝增加或移除大量質量，也會讓原本的調頻失準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A damper's design life often matches the building's, yet its performance drifts with changes in structural frequency, fluid ageing, hanger slack and temperature; renovations that add or remove large masses can also detune it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b066-v13-38","title":"長期性能、維護與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「監測與維護紀錄」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Monitoring and maintenance records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 μ = 0.0066、結構阻尼 1% 的雙自由度模型計算，最佳調頻時共振放大係數由 50 降到約 13.6（等效阻尼約 3.7%）；頻率比偏離 ±5% 時放大係數回升到約 23，等效阻尼約 2.1%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: In a two-degree-of-freedom model with μ = 0.0066 and 1% structural damping, optimum tuning lowers the resonant amplification from 50 to about 13.6 (equivalent damping about 3.7%); a ±5% frequency-ratio offset raises it back to about 23, an equivalent damping of about 2.1%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每年由監測資料重新辨識結構與擺錘頻率，計算頻率比是否仍在允收範圍（例如偏離 2% 以內）；定期抽驗阻尼器力—速度特性與吊索張力，並把結果寫入維護資料庫與原始基準比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Each year re-identify structural and pendulum frequencies from monitoring data and check that the frequency ratio stays within the acceptance range (for example within 2%); periodically spot-check damper force–velocity behaviour and hanger tension, and enter the results into a maintenance database for comparison with the original baseline.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 μ = 0.0066、結構阻尼 1% 的雙自由度模型計算，最佳調頻時共振放大係數由 50 降到約 13.6（等效阻尼約 3.7%）；頻率比偏離 ±5% 時放大係數回升到約 23，等效阻尼約 2.1%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"In a two-degree-of-freedom model with μ = 0.0066 and 1% structural damping, optimum tuning lowers the resonant amplification from 50 to about 13.6 (equivalent damping about 3.7%); a ±5% frequency-ratio offset raises it back to about 23, an equivalent damping of about 2.1%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長期性能、維護與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["質量塊越重，擺錘的擺動頻率就越低。","質量塊只要吊上樓層、掛上吊索就完成安裝，不需要荷重轉移計畫。","以 μ = 0.0066、結構阻尼 1% 的雙自由度模型計算，最佳調頻時共振放大係數由 50 降到約 13.6（等效阻尼約 3.7%）。"],"optionsEn":["The heavier the mass, the lower the pendulum frequency.","Once the mass is lifted and the hangers are attached, installation is complete without a load-transfer plan.","In a two-degree-of-freedom model with μ = 0.0066 and 1% structural damping, optimum tuning lowers the resonant amplification from 50 to about 13.6 (equivalent damping about 3.7%)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 μ = 0.0066、結構阻尼 1% 的雙自由度模型計算，最佳調頻時共振放大係數由 50 降到約 13.6（等效阻尼約 3.7%）；頻率比偏離 ±5% 時放大係數回升到約 23，等效阻尼約 2.1%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"In a two-degree-of-freedom model with μ = 0.0066 and 1% structural damping, optimum tuning lowers the resonant amplification from 50 to about 13.6 (equivalent damping about 3.7%); a ±5% frequency-ratio offset raises it back to about 23, an equivalent damping of about 2.1%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b066-v13-39","title":"長期性能、維護與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「監測與維護紀錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Monitoring and maintenance records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每年由監測資料重新辨識結構與擺錘頻率，計算頻率比是否仍在允收範圍（例如偏離 2% 以內）；定期抽驗阻尼器力—速度特性與吊索張力，並把結果寫入維護資料庫與原始基準比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Each year re-identify structural and pendulum frequencies from monitoring data and check that the frequency ratio stays within the acceptance range (for example within 2%); periodically spot-check damper force–velocity behaviour and hanger tension, and enter the results into a maintenance database for comparison with the original baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含操作與維護手冊、緊急鎖定程序、事件後檢查表、監測資料格式與聯絡窗口；大樓重大改裝或使用變更前，須由結構顧問評估對阻尼器調頻的影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include the operation and maintenance manual, emergency locking procedure, post-event checklist, monitoring data format and contacts; before major renovation or change of use, the structural consultant must assess the effect on damper tuning.","failure":"注意干擾：若交接時沒有留下調頻基準與試驗紀錄，多年後即使阻尼器已失準，管理單位也無法判斷，只能等住戶抱怨；大規模改裝未通知結構顧問，也可能使阻尼器在不知情下失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without tuning baselines and test records at handover, a damper can drift out of tune for years before anyone can tell, until occupants complain; major renovations made without notifying the structural consultant can silently defeat the damper. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每年由監測資料重新辨識結構與擺錘頻率，計算頻率比是否仍在允收範圍（例如偏離 2% 以內）；定期抽驗阻尼器力—速度特性與吊索張力，並把結果寫入維護資料庫與原始基準比較。","textEn":"Each year re-identify structural and pendulum frequencies from monitoring data and check that the frequency ratio stays within the acceptance range (for example within 2%); periodically spot-check damper force–velocity behaviour and hanger tension, and enter the results into a maintenance database for comparison with the original baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含操作與維護手冊、緊急鎖定程序、事件後檢查表、監測資料格式與聯絡窗口；大樓重大改裝或使用變更前，須由結構顧問評估對阻尼器調頻的影響。","textEn":"Handover should include the operation and maintenance manual, emergency locking procedure, post-event checklist, monitoring data format and contacts; before major renovation or change of use, the structural consultant must assess the effect on damper tuning.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長期性能、維護與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover\"?","options":["每年由監測資料重新辨識結構與擺錘頻率，計算頻率比是否仍在允收範圍（例如偏離 2% 以內）。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要量到頻率，阻尼比可以直接沿用設計假設。"],"optionsEn":["Each year re-identify structural and pendulum frequencies from monitoring data and check that the frequency ratio stays within the acceptance range (for example within 2%).","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Once the frequency is measured, the damping ratio can simply be taken from the design assumption."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每年由監測資料重新辨識結構與擺錘頻率，計算頻率比是否仍在允收範圍（例如偏離 2% 以內）；定期抽驗阻尼器力—速度特性與吊索張力，並把結果寫入維護資料庫與原始基準比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Each year re-identify structural and pendulum frequencies from monitoring data and check that the frequency ratio stays within the acceptance range (for example within 2%); periodically spot-check damper force–velocity behaviour and hanger tension, and enter the results into a maintenance database for comparison with the original baseline. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b066-v13-40","title":"長期性能、維護與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"prerequisiteIds":["b066-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「監測與維護紀錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Monitoring and maintenance records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若交接時沒有留下調頻基準與試驗紀錄，多年後即使阻尼器已失準，管理單位也無法判斷，只能等住戶抱怨；大規模改裝未通知結構顧問，也可能使阻尼器在不知情下失效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without tuning baselines and test records at handover, a damper can drift out of tune for years before anyone can tell, until occupants complain; major renovations made without notifying the structural consultant can silently defeat the damper. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此交接文件必須包含設計參數、調頻紀錄、試驗基準、檢查週期與允收範圍，並把長期監測資料定期與基準比對，偏離時啟動重新調頻或維修。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover documents must therefore contain design parameters, tuning records, test baselines, inspection intervals and acceptance ranges, and long-term monitoring data must be compared with the baseline periodically to trigger retuning or repair when they diverge.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器是被動裝置，裝好之後就不需要維護與監測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A damper is passive, so once installed it needs no maintenance or monitoring.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b066-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若交接時沒有留下調頻基準與試驗紀錄，多年後即使阻尼器已失準，管理單位也無法判斷，只能等住戶抱怨；大規模改裝未通知結構顧問，也可能使阻尼器在不知情下失效。","textEn":"Without tuning baselines and test records at handover, a damper can drift out of tune for years before anyone can tell, until occupants complain; major renovations made without notifying the structural consultant can silently defeat the damper.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]},{"id":"b066-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長期性能、維護與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-term performance, maintenance and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若交接時沒有留下調頻基準與試驗紀錄，多年後即使阻尼器已失準，管理單位也無法判斷，只能等住戶抱怨；大規模改裝未通知結構顧問，也可能使阻尼器在不知情下失效。","超高層擺動大就代表結構不夠強，必須加粗柱子。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without tuning baselines and test records at handover, a damper can drift out of tune for years before anyone can tell, until occupants complain.","Large sway in a supertall tower means it is not strong enough, so the columns must be thickened."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若交接時沒有留下調頻基準與試驗紀錄，多年後即使阻尼器已失準，管理單位也無法判斷，只能等住戶抱怨；大規模改裝未通知結構顧問，也可能使阻尼器在不知情下失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without tuning baselines and test records at handover, a damper can drift out of tune for years before anyone can tell, until occupants complain; major renovations made without notifying the structural consultant can silently defeat the damper. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-motioneering-taipei-101","v13s-motioneering-shanghai-tower","v13s-ctbuh-taipei-101","v13s-wiki-tuned-mass-damper"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
